\par\par \b \uc2 TIMELINE - A history of \uc2 G7\uc2 , G20 and  \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 1,075 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2017\par 11:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 LONDON, March 10 (Reuters) - Finance ministers and central bankers from the G20 group of leading industrialised nations meet in Germany next week for the first time since \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was elected president of the United States.\par \par \uc2 In light of recent comments from the White House about the dollar, global financial imbalances and world trade, it could be one of the most crucial gatherings in the four-decade history of G5, \uc2 G7\uc2  and G20 meetings.\par \par \uc2 Washington has accused Germany, Japan and China of exploiting exchange rate weakness for competitive advantage over the United States. And with Trump looking to make good on the protectionist, isolationist and "America First" platform he was elected on, G20 officials may struggle to present a united front on March 17-18 in Baden-Baden.\par \par \uc2 Below is a timeline tracing the history of cooperation between \uc2 G7\uc2  and latterly G20 countries on world trade and financial conventions - especially in relation to \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  - including direct, coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 March-October 2011 - \uc2 G7\uc2  nations jointly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March to stem yen strength when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  spikes against the dollar after a massive earthquake in \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 . This is \uc2 G7\uc2 's last coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. Tokyo then acts alone again in August and October.\par \par \uc2 September 2010 - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the first time in six years after the U.S. dollar hits a 15-year-low of 82.87 yen. Tokyo acts alone, but its move will have been tacitly approved at \uc2 G7\uc2  level.\par \par \uc2 March 2009 - G20 finance officials meet in Horsham, England, ahead of the leaders summit in London a few weeks later. With the world economy and financial system still reeling from the Lehman fallout, participants agree to take coordinated action to stimulate demand and employment. They also pledge to fight against all forms of protectionism. It is perhaps G20's high water mark - the low for world stock markets turns out to be in March, and the global economy begins to recover.\par \par \uc2 November 2008 - The first G20 leaders summit takes place in Washington under the banner "Financial Markets and the World Economy".\par \par \uc2 September 2008 - As the world economy and financial system plunges into crisis following the collapse of \uc2 Lehman Brothers\uc2 , \uc2 G7\uc2  pledges to "protect the integrity of the international financial system and facilitate liquid, smooth functioning markets". It stands ready "to take whatever actions may be necessary, individually and collectively, to ensure the stability of the international financial system."\par \par \uc2 September 2003 - In the midst of concerted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and China refusing to loosen the yuan's peg to the dollar, \uc2 G7\uc2  issues a strongly worded communique on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Dubai. It says "more flexibility in exchange rates is desirable for major countries or economic areas to promote smooth and widespread adjustments in the international financial system, based on market mechanisms."\par \par \uc2 May 2002-March 2004 - The \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly and in record amounts to curb the yen's rise, mostly alone but also on occasion with the \uc2 ECB\uc2  and Fed.\par \par \uc2 September 2001 - The BOJ on its own and with \uc2 ECB\uc2 , euro zone central banks and \uc2 New York Fed\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell yen for dollars, worrying about an export-crippling rise in the value of the yen following the 9/11 attacks.\par \par \uc2 September-November 2000 - Central banks in Europe, Japan and the United States, acting together for the first time since 1995, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to drive the euro higher after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits an all-time low below $0.8225, a loss of nearly 30 percent of its value since its January 1999 launch.\par \par \uc2 September 1999 - G20 finance ministers and central bankers meet for the first time under the banner of G20, "a group of countries representing both developed and emerging economies from every region of the globe (whose) purpose is to ensure broader participation in discussions on international financial affairs among countries whose size or strategic importance gives them a particularly crucial role in the global economy."\par \par \uc2 January 1999-April 2000 - Concerned that the strong yen will choke off a fragile economic recovery, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to tame its strength. The BOJ sells yen at least 18 times in this period, including once via the Fed and once via the \uc2 ECB\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 April-June 1998 - With the yen weakening, the BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . As the yen crumples below 144 to the dollar, U.S. authorities join the BOJ in June, spending $833 million buying yen.\par \par \uc2 April 1994-August 1995 - Dollar sinks to a record low against the German mark and a post-World-War Two low against the yen. From April 1994, the United States \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly, often with Japanese and European central banks, to prop up the greenback.\par \par \uc2 1991-1992 - U.S. and European central banks \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly after the Gulf War tips the U.S. economy into recession. Washington \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  on both sides of the market, buying and selling dollars.\par \par \uc2 1988-1990 - The dollar is back on the march again, and the United States \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  after \uc2 G7\uc2  statements on importance of maintaining exchange rate stability.\par \par \uc2 Feb. 22, 1987 - \uc2 G7\uc2  meet in Paris to halt a steep decline in the dollar's value in what becomes known as the "Louvre Accord". This comes only 17 months after the "Plaza Accord" that successfully brought an end to the dollar's surge in the early 1980s. Louvre does not trigger a rebound, but does herald several years of general stability, certainly relative to the inflation-busting and growth-fired period under then-president Ronald Reagan and Federal Reserve chairman Paul Volcker.\par \par \uc2 September 1985 - The G5 (Italy and Canada don't take part) meet in New York's Plaza Hotel to discuss the dollar's 80 percent surge under Reagan and Volcker. The rare agreement to bring the dollar down will become known as the "Plaza Accord". It works too - the dollar, already on the slide, falls 40 percent over the next year and a half.\par \par \uc2 1976 - Canada joins, making it the \uc2 G7\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 1975 - Italy joins, making it the G6. Finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors from these countries meet just outside Paris to discuss "current world issues in a frank and informal manner".\par \par \uc2 1974 - Senior finance officials from the United States, United Kingdom, France, West Germany and Japan meet informally for the first time under the guise of the "Group of Five", or G5. (Compiled by Jamie McGeever; Editing by Pritha Sarkar) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-3-10T11:58:09.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170310ed3a00edj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
