\par\par \b \uc2 Trump's  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Complaints Hit Unexpected Targets\b0\par\par\uc2 By Saumya Vaishampayan \par \uc2 708 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Februar 2017\par 09:47\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2017, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 HONG KONG--U.S. President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's accusations of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation appear to be reaching an audience he may not have primarily intended.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Trump vowed on the campaign trail to revive American manufacturing, in part by taking a hard line on Chinese trade practices and labeling the country a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator. Since taking office, the president has accused both China and Japan of consistently devaluing their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , while his top trade adviser Peter Navarro has accused Germany of benefiting from what he termed the "grossly undervalued" euro.\par \par \uc2 All three countries, which rank among the U.S.'s top five trading partners, have brushed off the Trump administration's claims.\par \par \uc2 "No one has the right to tell us that the yen is weak," Japan's finance minister \uc2 Taro Aso\uc2  told parliament on Wednesday, following last weekend's meeting between Mr. Trump and Prime Minister \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since 2011 following a major tsunami and resulting Fukushima nuclear disaster.\par \par \uc2 "The charge that Germany exploits the U.S. and other countries with an undervalued \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is more than absurd," \uc2 Jens Weidmann\uc2 , the president of the German \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said earlier this month.\par \par \uc2 China hasn't directly commented on Mr. Trump's criticisms, but most analysts say Beijing recently has been propping up the yuan by selling foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves rather than looking to weaken it.\par \par \uc2 Still, some smaller economies look like they are taking notice, notably Taiwan and Switzerland. The \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  found in October that both had engaged in persistent, one-way \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , essentially by buying foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  like the U.S. dollar and selling their own to maintain weak exchange rates.\par \par \uc2 Analysts say the central banks of Switzerland and Taiwan are now stepping back from those activities, perhaps to avoid closer scrutiny from the Trump administration. The upshot: The Swiss franc has advanced nearly 2% against the U.S. dollar this year, while the new Taiwan dollar has surged 5.3%. Both have outperformed the euro and yen since the U.S. election in early November.\par \par \uc2 Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought $500 million in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the fourth quarter, well below its quarterly average of more than $3 billion since 2012, according to Khoon Goh, head of Asia research at ANZ in Singapore, who said he suspects it is stepping back from "\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it doesn't comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.\par \par \uc2 For the first nine months of last year, the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to slow the franc's rise, spending an amount roughly equivalent to its current-account surplus for the period, \uc2 J.P. Morgan\uc2  analysts note. Over the following four months, the scale dropped to around two-thirds of the surplus.\par \par \uc2 "It's not an entirely fanciful suggestion that the SNB might be tapering \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in order to the guard against the risk of being cited by the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  as a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator," the analysts wrote in a note.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 For the U.S. to label an economy a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator under the current law, it must have a large trade surplus with the U.S. and a hefty current-account surplus and persistently \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in one direction. As of October, no economies met all three criteria.\par \par \uc2 Recent comments from officials in South Korea, which the Treasury has flagged for its hefty trade surplus with the U.S. and its current-account surplus, suggest they're similarly eager to avoid U.S. ire, says Govinda Finn, senior analyst at Standard Life Investments in Edinburgh. The Korean won has surged 5.2% against the dollar this year.\par \par \uc2 But any gains in the Korean and Taiwanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to U.S. political pressure may not last, he said: "On a longer-term horizon, there's a pretty strong case to say both of those \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  can and will weaken as the authorities look to support their economies."\par \par \uc2 Jenny W. Hsu contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Saumya Vaishampayan at saumya.vaishampayan@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 17, 2017 03:47 ET (08:47 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020170217ed2h000r6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
