\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 3-Japan policymakers reject Trump devaluation claims\b0\par\par\uc2 842 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2017\par 11:01\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2017 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Japan abiding by G7, G20 agreements - government spokesman\par \par \uc2 * BOJ not targeting \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  - top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat\par \par \uc2 * PM Abe defends BOJ policy as needed to reflate economy\par \par \uc2 * Japan sees no reason to be criticised by Trump\par \par \uc2 * Trump remarks won't bind BOJ's hands on policy - ex-BOJ's Momma (Adds comment from Abe, detail)\par \par \uc2 By Leika Kihara and Tetsushi Kajimoto\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Feb 1 (Reuters) - Japanese policymakers hit back on Wednesday at U.S. President Donald Trump's accusation of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation, stressing that Japan was abiding by a \uc2 Group of 20\uc2  agreement to refrain from competitive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation.\par \par \uc2 Prime Minister \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2  defended the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 's massive stimulus programme, saying it was intended to reflate the economy and was not \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation.\par \par \uc2 "Bold monetary easing is a necessary policy to accelerate economic growth and the United States is doing the same thing," Abe told parliament on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "If Japan's economy improves, that's not a bad thing for the United States," he said, adding that he will explain this point when he meets Trump next week.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was on the defensive after Trump and his trade adviser, Peter Navarro, on Tuesday criticised China, Germany and Japan, saying they were devaluing their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the disadvantage of the United States.\par \par \uc2 Senior Japanese officials, worried about the pain a rise in the yen could inflict on the export-reliant economy, scrambled to contain damage as the dollar hit a two-month low of 112.08 yen on Tuesday, following Trump's remarks.\par \par \uc2 The top government spokesman told reporters it was "absolutely not the case" that Japan was devaluing the yen to gain an unfair trade advantage.\par \par \uc2 "Japan is guiding policy in line with agreements made by the G7 and G20 countries. There will be no change to that stance," said Chief Cabinet Secretary \uc2 Yoshihide Suga\uc2 , one of Abe's closest aides and the point-person on economic policy.\par \par \uc2 Masatsugu Asakawa, Japan's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat, told reporters that exchange-rates were determined by markets and were not being manipulated.\par \par \uc2 "As Bank of Japan Governor (Haruhiko) Kuroda has said repeatedly, Japan's monetary policy aims to achieve the domestic purpose of ending deflation. It's not aimed at \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates," Asakawa, vice finance minister for international affairs, told reporters.\par \par \uc2 "If he is talking about \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't done any lately," he added, referring to Trump.\par \par \uc2 Kuroda later told parliament the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to promote "powerful monetary easing" to achieve its 2 percent inflation target as quickly as possible.\par \par \uc2 Trump's comments suggest that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy will be among main topics at talks between Trump and Abe in Washington on Feb. 10. Japanese media reported the two may hold another meeting in Florida the following day.\par \par \uc2 WON'T BIND BOJ?\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since November 2011. However, the weak yen has been considered one of the few successes of Abe's "Abenomics" stimulus policies aimed at pulling the economy out of two decades of deflation.\par \par \uc2 As one of three "arrows" of Abenomics, the BOJ adopted a massive asset-buying programme in 2013. It was praised for boosting exporters' profits and brightening business sentiment through a weak yen.\par \par \uc2 The yen has fallen 20 percent against the dollar since then, but is off its lows of around 125 yen to the dollar in 2015.\par \par \uc2 While the yen spiked in the middle of last year, as investors bought it as a safe haven against global risks, like Britain's decision to leave the \uc2 European Union\uc2 , it slid versus the dollar again as U.S. bond yields rose on market expectations of Trump's inflation-stoking policies.\par \par \uc2 Japanese policymakers have argued that the BOJ's ultra-easy monetary policy is solely aimed at beating deflation and did not go against a \uc2 Group of 20\uc2  agreement to refrain from using monetary policy for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation.\par \par \uc2 "There's no reason for the U.S. to criticize our \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and monetary policies," said a Japanese government official with knowledge of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.\par \par \uc2 Trump's comments are unlikely to bind the BOJ's hands on monetary policy, said Kazuo Momma, a former senior BOJ official, adding that policymakers would not consider easing unless the yen spiked well above 100 to the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "Trump's comments could continue to create short-term market volatility, but the BOJ shouldn't respond to each and every remark he makes," Momma, who retains close contact with incumbent policymakers, told Reuters.\par \par \uc2 Naoyuki Shinohara, a former \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  executive and previously Japan's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat, said pressure by Trump should not hinder any necessary monetary easing by the BOJ.\par \par \uc2 Asked whether yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could become an option if the yen kept rising in the wake of Trump's remarks, Shinohara said: "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  probably won't be too effective."\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Stanley White, Yoshifumi Takemoto, Hitoshi Ishida, Takashi Umekawa and Chris Gallagher; Editing by Lincoln Feast, Robert Birsel) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2017-2-1T11:01:49.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020170201ed21003xs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
