\par\par \b \uc2 Japan's Export Volume Rises at Fastest Pace in Nearly Two Years -- Update\b0\par\par\uc2 By Takashi Nakamichi \par \uc2 567 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Dezember 2016\par 07:10\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 TOKYO--Japan's export volume rose at the fastest pace in nearly two years in November, boosted by demand from China, signaling that the world's third-largest economy is on a steady growth track.\par \par \uc2 After suffering two years of choppy expansion that undercut Prime Minister \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2 's ambitions to revive the economy, figures this year suggest Japan is on a more solid footing. The economy expanded modestly in each of the first three quarters of 2016, and economists expect something similar in the fourth quarter.\par \par \uc2 Exports, which traditionally drive Japan's industrial growth, have turned from a drag to a tailwind recently, thanks to factors such as growing demand for Japanese parts from Chinese smartphone makers.\par \par \uc2 Japan's exports to China increased 4.4% from a year earlier to Yen1.1 trillion ($9.3 billion) during November, the first rise in value terms since February. Semiconductor maker \uc2 Toshiba Corp\uc2 .'s stock price has jumped 38% since the beginning of October.\par \par \uc2 Overall, export volume rose 7.4% in November from a year earlier, driven by demand for semiconductors, ships and car parts, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday.\par \par \uc2 The figures add to the likelihood that the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  will raise its assessment of Japan's economy, including export demand, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  concludes its regular two-day policy meeting on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 SMBC Nikko Securities\uc2  economist Junichi Makino said there was even a small chance that the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  would tighten monetary policy by raising its target for the interest rate on 10-year government bonds. The target currently stands at zero.\par \par \uc2 While Mr. Makino said he still expected the BOJ to stand pat, and other economists dismissed the chance of a rate increase, the discussion shows how the debate has shifted. Until recently, each BOJ meeting was preceded by speculation of possible new easing steps to jolt the lackluster economy.\par \par \uc2 Since \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's victory in the U.S. presidential election, the yen has fallen sharply and stock prices have moved to a high for the year. A weaker yen makes Japanese exporters more competitive and makes the country a more attractive destination for tourists, which bodes well for the economy in 2017.\par \par \uc2 Still, economists said Japan was vulnerable to any unexpected shifts in Mr. Trump's policies. He has criticized China for what he described as that nation's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation and might take a dim view of the yen's recent fall, said another SMBC Nikko Securities economist, Yoshimasa Maruyama.\par \par \uc2 "A further appreciation in the dollar wouldn't sit well with President-elect Trump's intentions," Mr. Maruyama said. "It's possible that he will try to correct the dollar's strength through verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Trump said during the campaign that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  was taking advantage of the U.S. by exporting many cars. According to Monday's data, Japan exported 180,919 vehicles to the U.S. in November, up 26% from the year-earlier figure. Meanwhile, Japan's imports fell nearly 9% in November, the 23rd consecutive month of contraction.\par \par \uc2 Another risk is a sudden downturn in China, where government efforts to restrain credit growth have triggered market volatility.\par \par \uc2 Write to Takashi Nakamichi at takashi.nakamichi@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 December 19, 2016 01:10 ET (06:10 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020161219eccj000fc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
