\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 2016\par 11:52\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Eurozone Recovery Remains Reliant on ECB Stimulus, Says \uc2 Mario Draghi\par \par \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President \uc2 Mario Draghi\uc2  sent a strong signal that the \uc2 ECB\uc2  will extend its bond-purchase program next month, warning that the eurozone economy remains heavily reliant on the \uc2 ECB\uc2 's stimulus measures.\par \par \uc2 Selloff Pulls Japanese Bond Yields Further Above Zero\par \par \uc2 A global government-bond selloff rolled into Asia on Friday after a two-day breather, putting the yield on Japan's benchmark 10-year government bond more firmly in positive territory.\par \par \uc2 Kuroda: BOJ Wanted to Counter 'Unusually Rapid' Yield Rises\par \par \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Gov. Haruhiko Kuroda said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the bond market the previous day because it wanted to suppress "unusually sharp" yield rises.\par \par \uc2 Trump Offers Flynn Role as National Security Adviser\par \par \uc2 President-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has offered the job of national security adviser to retired Lt. Gen. Michael Flynn, a person familiar with the process said Thursday, a move that would elevate a longtime officer who became known for criticizing the country's terrorism policies from inside the military.\par \par \uc2 Japan Finance Minister Welcomes Yen Weakening\par \par \uc2 Japan's finance minister on said the yen's recent weakening was a sign of returning stability.\par \par \uc2 Swiss Franc Still 'Significantly Overvalued,' Official Says\par \par \uc2 The Swiss franc remains "significantly overvalued," and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets as needed, a top official of the \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Japan's Abe Stresses Importance of Security Alliance at Trump Meeting\par \par \uc2 Japanese Prime Minister \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2  said he wants to establish an understanding with U.S. President-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  about the importance of the nations' security alliance\par \par \uc2 Greek Finance Minister Urges Quick Deal on Debt Relief\par \par \uc2 Euclid Tsakalotos, in an interview, warned that creditors must agree on a debt restructuring in coming weeks or miss the best chance to bring his country's seven-year crisis to an end.\par \par \uc2 U.N. Envoy Urges Europe to Avoid Australia's 'Cruel' Migrant Model\par \par \uc2 The United Nations' top human rights envoy condemned Australia's system of offshore detention for asylum seekers as "cruel, inhuman and degrading."\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 November 18, 2016 05:52 ET (10:52 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020161118ecbi0018x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
