\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked for November 18\b0\par\par\uc2 869 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 2016\par 07:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asian-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0600 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Japan's Shinzo Abe Discusses Security Alliance at Meeting With \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 President-elect \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Thursday held his first face-to-face talks with a foreign leader since the election, meeting with Japanese Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shinzo Abe\f28 \uc2 \f2  in New York for a 90-minute session sought by the visiting Mr. Abe to gauge Mr. Trump's views on the nations' security alliance. (published 0458 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ Gov Kuroda: Wanted to Counter 'Unusually Rapid' Yield Rises by Fixed-Rate Purchases \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Gov. Haruhiko Kuroda said Friday that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the bond market the previous day because it wanted to suppress "unusually sharp" yield rises (published 0402 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Japan's Finance Minister Welcomes Yen's Sharp Weakening as Sign of Stability \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister on Friday said the yen's recent weakening was a sign of returning stability, welcoming a reversal in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's uptrend sparked by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2 's win in the U.S. presidential election. (published 0316 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Negara Malaysia\f28 \uc2 \f2  'Stepped In' to Defend Ringgit \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has entered markets to defend the ringgit after the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened more than 4% against the U.S dollar following \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2 's victory in the U.S. presidential election last week, its assistant governor said Friday. (published 0512 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par China New Home Price Rise Slows in Oct as Cooling Steps Take Hold \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Average home prices in China rose at a slower pace in October from the month before, signaling that recent cooling measures have helped curb frothy prices in major cities. (published 0236 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Philippines Approves $4.46 Bln in Infrastructure, Agriculture Projects \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Philippines' \f28 \uc2 \f2 National Economic and Development Authority\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday that the eight agriculture and infrastructure projects approved by its board this week will cost a total 221.89 billion pesos . (published 0233 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Changsha Pilot Investment Holdings Plans USD-Denominated Bond Offering -- Document \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Changsha Pilot Investment Holdings Co., a local-government financial vehicle in China's Hunan province, is planning a U.S. dollar-denominated bond offering, according to a mandate document seen Friday by The Wall Street Journal. (published 0234 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par China Energy Reserve & Chemicals Raises US$265 Million via USD Bond Sale -- Term Sheet \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Energy Reserve & Chemicals Group Co. raised US$265 million from a U.S. dollar-denominated bond offering for general corporate purposes via an offshore unit, according to a term sheet seen Friday by The Wall Street Journal. (published 0343 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par South Korea Blocks Google From Expanding Local Maps -- Update \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 South Korea denied a request by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Alphabet Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s \f28 \uc2 \f2 Google\f28 \uc2 \f2  to export digital-map data from the country, effectively blocking the U.S. technology giant from expanding its limited local-map services there. (published 0551 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Coca-Cola\f28 \uc2 \f2  to Divest Itself of China Bottling for Roughly $1 Billion \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Coca-Cola Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Thursday it reached a definitive agreement to divest its bottling stakes in China for roughly $1 billion, part of broader strategy to focus on its more profitable concentrate-making business. (published 0126 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Japan's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Peach Aviation\f28 \uc2 \f2  Orders 13 Airbus Commercial Planes \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese low-cost carrier \f28 \uc2 \f2 Peach Aviation\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Friday it has ordered a total of 13 commercial aircraft from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Airbus Group SE\f28 \uc2 \f2  in a deal that could be worth more than $1 billion. (published 0154 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par China Evergrande Raises its Stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Vanke\f28 \uc2 \f2  to 9.452% \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Evergrande Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  has spent a total of around 22.26 billion yuan for a 9.452% stake in rival \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Vanke Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . as of Thursday. (published 0131 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Huadian Power International\f28 \uc2 \f2 : Vice Chairman Chen Jianhua Resigns \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Energy firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 Huadian Power International Corp. Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said late Thursday vice chairman Chen Jianhua has resigned with immediate effect. (published 0142 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Starmalls 9-Month Net Profit Up 53% on Year at PHP1.1 Billion \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Starmalls Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Friday that its net profit in the nine months through September surged 53% on year to 1.1 billion pesos as it continued to expand its shopping mall network on the back of strong consumer spending. (published 0131 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par LEAP Holdings Sees Substantial Drop in April-September Profit \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Construction firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 LEAP Holdings Group Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said late Thursday it expects a substantial decrease in profit for April-September from a year earlier, partly due to weaker revenue from foundation business. (published 0127 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Yida China Controlling Shareholder to Sell 53.02% Stake for HK$3.01 Billion \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yida China Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 .'s controlling shareholder, Sun Yinhuan, has agreed to sell a major stake to a unit of China Minsheng Jiaye Investment Co. for 3.01 billion Hong Kong dollars . (published 0124 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Asia Shares Rise as Weaker Yen Sends Nikkei to 10-Month High -- Update \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 A weaker yen sent Japan's Nikkei to a 10-month high on Friday, helping drive gains across key Asian markets as robust U.S. economic data buoyed expectations of an interest-rate increase next month. (published 0446 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 November 18, 2016 01:15 ET (06:15 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020161118ecbi000gx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
