\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 2016\par 07:15\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japan's Shinzo Abe Discusses Security Alliance at Meeting With \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 President-elect \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  on Thursday held his first face-to-face talks with a foreign leader since the election, meeting with Japanese Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Shinzo Abe\f28 \uc2 \f2  in New York for a 90-minute session sought by the visiting Mr. Abe to gauge Mr. Trump's views on the nations' security alliance. (published 0458 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ Gov Kuroda: Wanted to Counter 'Unusually Rapid' Yield Rises by Fixed-Rate Purchases \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Gov. Haruhiko Kuroda said Friday that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the bond market the previous day because it wanted to suppress "unusually sharp" yield rises (published 0402 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Japan's Finance Minister Welcomes Yen's Sharp Weakening as Sign of Stability \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's finance minister on Friday said the yen's recent weakening was a sign of returning stability, welcoming a reversal in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's uptrend sparked by \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2 's win in the U.S. presidential election. (published 0316 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank Negara Malaysia\f28 \uc2 \f2  'Stepped In' to Defend Ringgit \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has entered markets to defend the ringgit after the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened more than 4% against the U.S dollar following \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2 's victory in the U.S. presidential election last week, its assistant governor said Friday. (published 0512 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Michael Flynn\f28 \uc2 \f2  Offered Role as \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2 's National Security Adviser -- 2nd Update \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 President-elect \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  has offered the job of national security adviser to retired Lt. Gen. Michael Flynn, people familiar with the process said Thursday, a move that would elevate a longtime officer who became known for criticizing the country's terrorism policies from inside the military. (published 0456 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par China Energy Reserve & Chemicals Raises US$265 Million via USD Bond Sale -- Term Sheet \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 China Energy Reserve & Chemicals Group Co. raised US$265 million from a U.S. dollar-denominated bond offering for general corporate purposes via an offshore unit, according to a term sheet seen Friday by The Wall Street Journal. (published 0343 GMT) \f28 \par \par \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 November 18, 2016 01:15 ET (06:15 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020161118ecbi000jn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
