\par\par \b \uc2 *Japan MOF Asakawa: Will Take Appropriate Action Against Speculative, Excessive  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Movements\b0\par\par\uc2 370 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 November 2016\par 07:38\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 9 Nov 2016 01:38 ET *Japan MOF Asakawa: Watching \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Markets With Close Attention\par \par \uc2 9 Nov 2016 01:39 ET *\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  MOF Asakawa: No Comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  Market \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 9 Nov 2016 01:39 ET *\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  MOF Asakawa: Not Ruling Out Any Action Against Stronger Yen\par \par \uc2 9 Nov 2016 01:40 ET *Japan MOF Asakawa: No G-7 Action Planned at This Point\par \par \uc2 9 Nov 2016 02:15 ET  Japan Ready to Act Against Excessive Yen Movements, Says Senior MOF Official\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Megumi Fujikawa and Mayumi Negishi \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 TOKYO--The Japanese government stands ready to take action against excessive rises in the yen, the nation's top \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  diplomat said Wednesday, following an emergency meeting of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and finance ministry officials as incoming results for the U.S. presidential election caused market turbulence.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "There have been volatile movements in the markets including \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates," said Masatsugu Asakawa, vice finance minister for international affairs.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 While he declined to make a comment on the possibility of direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , he said the ministry would take necessary action if excessive rises in the yen continued. He added that he wouldn't rule out any options in correcting such moves.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Mr. Asakawa spoke after the meeting with top officials from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  and the Financial Services Agency. The meeting was held after large swings in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and stock markets during Wednesday's trading as the likelihood grew of Republican \f28 \uc2 \f2 Donald Trump\f28 \uc2 \f2  winning the U.S. presidential election.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "We will monitor market movements in close cooperation with the government," said BOJ Executive Director \f28 \uc2 \f2 Masayoshi Amamiya\f28 \uc2 \f2 , who also attended the meeting.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The greenback briefly hit a low of Y101.19 Wednesday afternoon as election results came in, down sharply from a high of Y105.48 little more than four hours earlier. The dollar is now at Y102.42.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Nikkei Stock Average suffered its biggest percentage drop since the U.K. voted to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 .\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Write to Megumi Fujikawa and Mayumi Negishi at megumi.fujikawa@wsj.com, mayumi.negishi@wsj.com\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 November 09, 2016 02:15 ET (07:15 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020161109ecb9000u9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
