\par\par \b \uc2 USD/SGD Pressured as Yen Strengthens Toward 100.00 -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 163 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 September 2016\par 02:41\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 0041 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] USD/SGD is under pressure, and may retreat to the 1.3527 entrance of the daily Bollinger downtrend channel, as lead indicator the Japanese yen strengthens early Monday. The yen is a key component of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket used by the Singapore's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to manage the value of its dollar. USD/JPY has fallen back under the 101.00 mark and continues to fade lower, which might trigger fresh jawboning from Japanese officials. Last week, when the yen approached the 100.00 psychological barrier, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  took notice, and warned of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which sparked a two-day surge in USD/JPY that pulled USD/SGD and other regional pairs higher. USD/SGD is now 1.3579 from its Friday closing of 1.3589. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 September 25, 2016 20:41 ET (00:41 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160926ec9q00038\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
