\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-As yen rises, Japan MOF, FSA, BOJ set to meet at 0450 GMT to exchange views\b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 2016\par 06:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Yen edges toward 7-week high vs dollar               \par \par \uc2 * Japan policymakers prefer weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for exports, inflation               \par \par \uc2 * Options limited as G7 discourages competitive devaluation   (Adds details, context)               \par \par \uc2 By Stanley White and Kaori Kaneko               \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Aug 18 (Reuters) - \uc2 Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Financial Services Agency and the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  will hold a meeting at 1:50 p.m. (0450 GMT) to exchange views on financial markets as the yen edges toward a seven-week high versus the dollar.               \par \par \uc2 The MOF, the FSA and the BOJ announced the meeting in a joint statement earlier on Thursday, after \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  diplomat made a veiled threat to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in response to the yen moves \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  deems excessive.               \par \par \uc2 Policymakers tend to worry when the yen rises, because it curbs exports and increases deflationary pressure by lowering import prices, but some traders say there are few options available because \uc2 Group of Seven\uc2  countries frown on competitive devaluation.               \par \par \uc2 The yen edged up 0.2 percent to 100.10 per dollar. It rose as high as 99.645 at one point, nearing a seven-week peak of 99.55 to the dollar set on Tuesday, due to receding expectations for near-term U.S. interest rate hikes.               \par \par \uc2 Japan will act appropriately if there are any excessive moves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and will monitor markets closely, Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs, Masatsugu Asakawa told reporters earlier on Thursday.               \par \par \uc2 Members of the MOF, FSA and BOJ regularly meet to discuss financial markets.               \par \par \uc2 The yen has risen around 20 percent versus the dollar this year, which is weighing on exports and threatening to undermine business confidence.                                             \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-8-18T05:14:43.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160818ec8i007n1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
