\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Australian dollar sags on S&P outlook cut, yen firms\b0\par\par\uc2 904 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juli 2016\par 05:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved.  \par \par \uc2 * S&P cuts outlook on Australia's rating to negative from stable\par \par \uc2 * Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firms, but still shy of post-Brexit highs\par \par \uc2 * Sterling nurses losses after this week's slide to 31-year lows\par \par \uc2 * Fed held rates steady to assess Brexit impact, minutes show\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, July 7 (Reuters) - The Australian dollar withered after \uc2 Standard and Poor's\uc2  cut the outlook for that country's credit rating to negative on Thursday, while the safe-haven yen firmed in the fallout from Britain's vote last month to exit the \uc2 European Union\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Aussie fell as low as $0.7467, from an earlier session high of $0.7539, after S&P downgraded the outlook on Australia's AAA credit rating to negative from stable. But the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pared losses to last buy $0.7507, down 0.1 percent on the day.\par \par \uc2 The ratings agency had warned that deadlock on government policy after Saturday's inconclusive elections could endanger Australia's rating over the long run.\par \par \uc2 A Reuters poll taken ahead of S&P's move showed that analysts had raised their outlooks for the Australian and New Zealand dollars due to those countries' relatively high bond rates and the British pound's recent plunge.\par \par \uc2 The euro slipped 0.5 percent to 111.92 yen, but managed to hold above its Wednesday low of 110.84 and a 3 1/2-year low of 109.30 logged soon after the results of the Brexit referendum were apparent.\par \par \uc2 The dollar shed 0.4 percent to 100.95 yen, though it also remained above the previous session's low of 100.20 as well as its June 24 nadir of 99.000 hit after the UK's vote.\par \par \uc2 "There's a lot of nervousness. Post-Brexit issues are starting to sink in," said Jeff Kravetz, senior investment strategist at the Private Client Reserve at U.S. Bank in Scottsdale, Arizona.\par \par \uc2 "The yen has been a big story. It keeps strengthening as a safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said, adding that the dollar might break under 100 yen again against the backdrop of uncertainty.\par \par \uc2 Sharp yen gains are usually followed by verbal warnings from Japanese financial officials, one of whom said on Wednesday that the finance ministry was closely watching the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to see if any speculative factors were behind market moves.\par \par \uc2 According to Japan Macro Advisors' probability model of the risk of direct \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the dollar's fall to 95 yen could be a trigger point in the next 2 months, while from September onward, the threshold would shift to 90 yen.\par \par \uc2 "The Japanese yen is appreciating from an extremely weak level and the yen has to appreciate much further before Japan could gain an implicit approval from other G7 countries," said Takuji Okubo, chief economist at \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Macro Advisors.\par \par \uc2 "Past episodes of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  suggest a unilateral \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  without implicit approval from other G7 tends to be ineffective," Okubo said in a note.\par \par \uc2 Bank of Japan Governor Haruhiko Kuroda said on Thursday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to expand monetary stimulus further if needed to achieve its 2 percent inflation target, but he made no mention of the Brexit vote that has spread turmoil in financial markets.\par \par \uc2 Beleaguered sterling fell as low as 128.81 yen on Wednesday, its lowest since November 2012. It was last down 0.2 percent at 130.70.\par \par \uc2 The pound had skidded to $1.2798 in the previous session to log a fresh 31-year low, but was last up 0.1 percent at $1.2939.\par \par \uc2 Sterling remains under pressure despite the efforts of Bank of England Governor \uc2 Mark Carney\uc2 , who has attempted to calm investors roiled by Brexit with an unusually explicit signal that the Bank was poised to pump more stimulus into the economy in the coming months.\par \par \uc2 "People are still selling into sterling rallies, whenever it rises on any of the crosses," said Kaneo Ogino, director at \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research firm Global-info Co in Tokyo.\par \par \uc2 "The BOE might come up with some supportive measures," he said.\par \par \uc2 The BOE's next interest rate decision will come on July 14, though economists polled by Reuters mostly predicted that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would wait to cut interest rates until its meeting on Aug. 4, when it will likely have a clearer idea about Brexit's impact.\par \par \uc2 Fanning fears of financial contagion in the wake of the Brexit vote, the number of British property funds suspended in recent weeks doubled to six on Wednesday, leaving 15 billion pounds ($19.37 billion) frozen in the biggest seizing up of investment funds since the 2008 financial crisis.\par \par \uc2 Minutes of the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 's June policy meeting released on Wednesday showed that policymakers decided to keep interest rate hikes on hold as they assessed the Brexit impact.\par \par \uc2 The dollar was lifted overnight when \uc2 Institute for Supply Management\uc2  data revealed that growth in the U.S. economy's service sector increased in June at its fastest pace in seven months.\par \par \uc2 Investors awaited the key U.S. non-farm payrolls numbers due on Friday, which are expected to show employers added 180,000 jobs last month, according to a preliminary Reuters poll. That would follow May's surprisingly weak reading of just 38,000, which some economists expect to be revised upward. \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-7-7T04:17:44.000Z  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160707ec77005en\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
