\par\par \b \uc2 INTERVIEW- \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  should not give up right to  \highlight22\uc2 intervene \highlight\uc2  if yen rises sharply\b0\par\par\uc2 494 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 2016\par 10:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has right to smooth extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves\par \par \uc2 * BOJ should respond if jobs market worsens\par \par \uc2 TOKYO, June 28 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  should not give up the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if the yen sharply rises as it will threaten the nation's economy, a key economic adviser to Prime Minister \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2  said on Tuesday, after Britain's vote to exit the \uc2 European Union\uc2  caused market turmoil.\par \par \uc2 Koichi Hamada, an emeritus professor of economics at Yale University, told Reuters the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 's monetary policy was working but stimulus steps should be expanded if the yen firms further, thus, hurting the economy.\par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  should not give up the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in extreme situations, namely when the yen rises sharply," said Hamada, a special adviser to the Cabinet.\par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market in 2011 to restrain the strong yen.\par \par \uc2 The yen firmed to 99.00 yen per dollar on Friday, its strongest against the dollar since November 2013 as investors flocked to the safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the wake of Brexit. It was trading around 102.00 yen on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 He said the United States may not like weakening of the yen for Japan's own economic prosperity, nor would Washington be happy if Japan's monetary policy influences exchange rates.\par \par \uc2 "Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has the right to smooth extreme exchange rate fluctuations by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and influence over the course of exchange rate by monetary policy pursuing its macroeconomic objectives," he said.\par \par \uc2 He added that \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be restricted to counter abnormal moves that are regarded as created by speculators.\par \par \uc2 Shockwave on financial markets after the Brexit vote appeared to have subsided this week but Japanese policymakers remain ready to respond to a further sudden jump in the yen.\par \par \uc2 But markets are sceptical about \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market due to strong opposition from Washington.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Treasury Secretary Jack Lew said on Monday that market impact from Brexit has been orderly so far and unilateral action to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be inappropriate.\par \par \uc2 "I think \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and stock markets overreacted to the shock caused by Brexit. I think the real effects of Brexit in the long run would not be as big as people fear now," Hamada said.\par \par \uc2 Group of Seven\uc2  finance leaders vowed on Friday to continue to consult closely on market moves and financial stability and cooperate as appropriate, after Britain voted to exit the \uc2 European Union\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The BOJ held off fresh easing last month but many analysts expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will adopt additional stimulus at its next policy meeting on July 28-29.\par \par \uc2 "If the job market deteriorates, the BOJ should respond with appropriate policy measures regardless of what the \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  says," Hamada said.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Kaori Kaneko, Sumio Ito and Chang-Ran Kim; Editing by Jacqueline Wong)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-7-1T08:00:50.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160628ec6s00c1e\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
