\par\par \b \uc2 Japan LDP policy chief says bold steps needed to stem yen rise after Brexit - NHK\b0\par\par\uc2 239 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Juni 2016\par 07:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, June 26 (Reuters) - Japan's ruling Liberal Democratic Party's policy chief said on Sunday the government should take bold steps to respond to yen surges following Britain's decision to leave the \uc2 European Union\uc2 , the latest sign the government may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem yen rises.\par \par \uc2 "Speculative, violent moves (in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market) have extremely negative effects. If necessary, the government should not hesitate to respond, including \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Tomomi Inada, who represents \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ruling party's stance on policy issues, during a debate with policy chiefs from other parties aired by broadcaster NHK, according to the Nikkei daily.\par \par \uc2 Japan's financial markets have been on high alert after the safe-haven yen firmed to 99.00 yen per dollar on Friday following the Brexit vote - the first time the dollar dropped below the 100 yen mark since late 2013. This prompted Japanese Finance Minister \uc2 Taro Aso\uc2  to warn on Friday that the government will respond as needed to "extremely nervous" \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves.\par \par \uc2 Inada's comment also comes a day after an emergency meeting of senior officials from \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2 , the Financial Services Agency, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  to discuss financial markets post-Brexit, in which they said they would continue to closely coordinate moves and monitor markets. (Editing by Sam Holmes) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-6-26T06:56:43.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160626ec6q005bp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
