\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 675 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2016\par 08:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 'Brexit' Expected to Rattle U.S. Economy, Shake Its Influence \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Britain's exit is expected to jolt the U.S. economy, likely rattling restive equity markets and driving up the value of the dollar. It could also weaken U.S. diplomatic leverage in Europe and upend the corporate strategies of U.S. companies based in London. (published 0450 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Pound, Euro Tumble, Yen Strengthens as U.K. Votes to Leave EU - Update \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The U.K. pound tumbled to a three-decade low and the euro also weakened, while the yen strengthened in extremely choppy Asian trade Friday, as the U.K. vote to leave the the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  rattled global financial markets that had expected a 'remain' vote. (published 0543 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par German Foreign Minister Says U.K. Brexit Vote a Sad Day for Europe \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 German Foreign Minister Frank-Walter Steinmeier said the U.K.'s apparent decision to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  is sobering news. (published 0506 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par India Government Moves to Calm Markets \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's finance ministry\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Friday that the country's economic fundamentals and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves were strong enough to deal with any eventuality as a result of the U.K.'s exit from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 , seeking to calm investors amid a sharp decline in shares and the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0503 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par U.K. Projected to Leave European Union \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Britons voted to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 , U.K. broadcasters forecast, a startling rebuke that threatens to spark political turmoil in the U.K., weaken a continent already strained by multiple crises and rattle global financial markets (published 0448 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ Gov Kuroda: BOJ Stands Ready to Provide Sufficient Liquidity Including Swap Lines Among 6 Central Banks \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Gov. Haruhiko Kuroda said Friday that the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is prepared to take action, such as liquidity provision, against any shocks that may be caused by the result of the U.K. referendum. (published 0446 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOE's Carney To Speak Friday Morning -- Source \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of England Gov. Mark Carney will make a statement early Friday following the U.K.'s vote to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 , according to a person familiar with the matter. (published 0428 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Singapore May Industrial Output Up 0.9%, Misses Estimates \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's industrial production slowed in May on lower output growth in the electronics and pharmaceuticals sectors. (published 0500 GMT) \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Finance Minister Renews \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Threat as Yen Soars \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister said Friday that he will take "firm action if necessary" to stem the yen's advance, reiterating his willingness to undertake direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as the reported results of a U.K. referendum sent the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  soaring to multi-year highs. (published 0432 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Thailand Posts $1.53 Billion Trade Surplus in May, Despite Rising Imports \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand posted a trade surplus of $1.538 billion in May, more than doubling the $721 million recorded a month earlier, the Ministry of Commerce said Friday. (published 0407 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Japan MOF Asakawa: Will Consider Response to Rough Yen Movements With Fin Min \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's top \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bureaucrat said Friday that the yen's movement over the past few hours has been "unusually rough," signaling his concern over high volatility fueled by uncertainties over a U.K. referendum. (published 0306 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Japan Govt Seko: Will Carefully Watch Market Movements \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Deputy Chief Cabinet Secretary Hiroshige Seko said Friday that the government will carefully watch the impact of the U.K.'s referendum on financial markets, including the yen. (published 0249 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par U.K. Exit Heightens Fears of Disintegration \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The British exit of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  after more than four decades of membership delivers a shock to the rest of Europe and the wider Western world. (published 0421 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par ======= DOW JONES NEWSWIRES ANALYSIS AND COMMENTARIES ======= \par  \par 'Brexit' Collateral Damage Puts Japan in Hot Seat -- Heard on the Street \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The first wave of "Brexit" damage has made a major hit: Japan. (published 0503 GMT) \f28 \par \par \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 24, 2016 02:00 ET (06:00 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160624ec6o000nn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw20