\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked for June 24\b0\par\par\uc2 719 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2016\par 08:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asian-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0600 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par India Government Moves to Calm Markets \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 India's finance ministry\f28 \uc2 \f2  said on Friday that the country's economic fundamentals and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  reserves were strong enough to deal with any eventuality as a result of the U.K.'s exit from the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 , seeking to calm investors amid a sharp decline in shares and the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . (published 0503 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ Gov Kuroda: BOJ Stands Ready to Provide Sufficient Liquidity Including Swap Lines Among 6 Central Banks \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Gov. Haruhiko Kuroda said Friday that the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is prepared to take action, such as liquidity provision, against any shocks that may be caused by the result of the U.K. referendum. (published 0446 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Singapore May Industrial Output Up 0.9%, Misses Estimates \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Singapore's industrial production slowed in May on lower output growth in the electronics and pharmaceuticals sectors. (published 0500 GMT) \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Finance Minister Renews \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Threat as Yen Soars \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister said Friday that he will take "firm action if necessary" to stem the yen's advance, reiterating his willingness to undertake direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as the reported results of a U.K. referendum sent the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  soaring to multi-year highs. (published 0432 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Thailand Posts $1.53 Billion Trade Surplus in May, Despite Rising Imports \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand posted a trade surplus of $1.538 billion in May, more than doubling the $721 million recorded a month earlier, the Ministry of Commerce said Friday. (published 0407 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Japan MOF Asakawa: Will Consider Response to Rough Yen Movements With Fin Min \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's top \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bureaucrat said Friday that the yen's movement over the past few hours has been "unusually rough," signaling his concern over high volatility fueled by uncertainties over a U.K. referendum. (published 0306 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Japan Govt Seko: Will Carefully Watch Market Movements \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japan's Deputy Chief Cabinet Secretary Hiroshige Seko said Friday that the government will carefully watch the impact of the U.K.'s referendum on financial markets, including the yen. (published 0249 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Tata Sons\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ordered to Pay \f28 \uc2 \f2 NTT DoCoMo\f28 \uc2 \f2  $1.17 Billion in Damages -- Update \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NTT DoCoMo Inc\f28 \uc2 \f2 . on said an arbitration panel ordered \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tata Sons Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the holding company of Indian conglomerate \f28 \uc2 \f2 Tata Group\f28 \uc2 \f2 , to pay $1.17 billion in damages to the Japanese mobile carrier for breaching a shareholder agreement. (published 0305 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par South Korea Prosecutors Arrest Volkswagen Executive \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 An executive of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Volkswagen AG\f28 \uc2 \f2 's South Korean unit has been arrested amid widening investigations into the German auto maker's emissions-test cheating scandal. (published 0313 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bloomberry Resorts\f28 \uc2 \f2  Sells Controlling Stake in Jeju Hotel \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bloomberry Resorts Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said it sold its controlling stake in Jeju Sun Hotel & Casino in South Korea for 117.5 billion Korean won, a blow to the overseas expansion dreams of the Philippine gaming company. (published 0238 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Far East Consortium Full-Year Net Profit HK$734 Million \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Far East Consortium International Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . reported a 23.3% decline in net profit for the year ended March on lower property sales. (published 0041 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Oriental Watch Swings to Full-Year Loss of HK$15.5 Million \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Oriental Watch Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . swung to a net loss for the full year ended March amid sluggish retail sentiment due to a reduced number of mainland Chinese tourists visiting Hong Kong and Macau during the year. (published 0025 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Asian Shares Plummet on U.K. Vote for 'Brexit' -- 3rd Update \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Stocks in Japan suffered their worst day in five years, leading broad losses in markets across Asia while gold surged as results from the U.K.'s referendum on its \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  membership showed the country had voted to leave the trading bloc. (published 0456 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Oil Prices Drop by 6% As 'Leave' Camp leads in 'Brexit' Vote \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude-oil prices slid more than 6% in midday Asian trade Friday, their lowest in a week, as preliminary results of the U.K. "Brexit" referendum showed a lead for those wishing to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0351 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 24, 2016 02:03 ET (06:03 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160624ec6o000nu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
