\par\par \b \uc2 RPT- \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Sterling hits 31-year low on Brexit, central banks hint at  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 794 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2016\par 14:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Repeats to additional subscribers)\par \par \uc2 * Sterling falls 10 pct to lowest since before 1985 Plaza Accord\par \par \uc2 * Yen slips as \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  hints at possible action\par \par \uc2 * SNB confirms \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Swiss franc off highs\par \par \uc2 By Anirban Nag\par \par \uc2 LONDON, June 24 (Reuters) - Sterling sank 10 percent in value to its weakest since before the 1985 Plaza Accord on Friday after Britain voted to leave the \uc2 European Union\uc2 , triggering a global rush of capital into the traditional security of the yen and the Swiss franc.\par \par \uc2 Alongside the biggest moves in the pound in living memory the euro, which is expected to struggle given worries about the impact of a "Brexit" on the euro zone economy, also dropped sharply against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 The franc surged to its strongest in almost a year against the euro, and the yen to its highest in more than two years. The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  became the first major \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step in to drive down the value of the franc, while speculation that the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  could also act limited the yen's advance.\par \par \uc2 Japanese Finance Minister \uc2 Taro Aso\uc2  said Prime Minister \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2  had instructed him to cooperate with the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  and closely consult with \uc2 Group of Seven\uc2  partners in responding to market moves. Aso added that excess volatility in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets was undesirable and he would respond to market moves when necessary.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 German finance ministry\uc2  spokesman said finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chiefs from the G7 economic powers held a teleconference on Friday as Britain's decision to leave the \uc2 EU\uc2  created ripples in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and beyond.\par \par \uc2 The pound fell more than 10 percent to $1.3228, its lowest since before the world's major economies signed a deal to weaken the dollar in September 1985.\par \par \uc2 By 1150 GMT, it recovered to trade at $1.37, still 7.8 percent lower on the day, with traders citing Bank of England chief \uc2 Mark Carney\uc2 's comments that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stood ready to provide extra support as a reason for the bounce.\par \par \uc2 But Scottish First Minister \uc2 Nicola Sturgeon\uc2  gave markets another knock by saying a new referendum on breaking up the United Kingdom itself was now highly likely, leaving sterling vulnerable to further bouts of selling.\par \par \uc2 Earlier, British Prime Minister \uc2 David Cameron\uc2 , who campaigned to stay in the \uc2 EU\uc2 , said he will step down by October. Analysts expect months of economic and political turmoil which will dwarf the pressure on UK markets following sterling's "Black Wednesday" in 1992 when Britain was forced out of the pre-euro Exchange Rate Mechanism.\par \par \uc2 "The UK has voted to leave the \uc2 EU\uc2  and this decision hits the British economy at a difficult time," said Hans Redeker, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2 , adding investors' attention will shift to Britain's large current account deficit and that economic growth is likely to weaken. \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  expects it to fall to between $1.25 and $1.30.\par \par \uc2 Leading UK bank \uc2 HSBC\uc2  also cut its quarter end and year-end forecasts for sterling. It expects sterling to fall to $1.25 by the end of third-quarter and then to $1.20 by the end of 2016. It also cut its forecast for the euro for the end of the year to $1.10 from $1.20 previously.\par \par \uc2 EURO LOWER\par \par \uc2 The euro was under pressure against most other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as investors worried Brexit could fuel anti-establishment movements in other European countries. A new election is planned in Spain on Sunday after an inconclusive vote last December.\par \par \uc2 The euro fell to $1.0912, a low last seen in March, before recovering to $1.1050, still down 2.9 percent on the day. It fell nearly 2 percent against the franc, before recovering to trade 1.1 percent lower at 1.0891 francs.\par \par \uc2 Demand for the safe-haven yen has grown steadily with Brexit anxiety over the past month. The greenback dropped to as low as 99 yen, a fall of 6.7 percent, before gaining to 102.40 yen, still on track for its biggest one-day drop since late 1998.\par \par \uc2 The rise in the yen kept alive the risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Japanese and perhaps even coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \uc2 Group of Seven\uc2  countries in coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 "In the next week or two, it would be naive not to expect central banks to be in the market trying to smooth price movements," said Stewart Richardson, chief investment manager at RMG Wealth Management, adding investors are likely to stay away from riskier \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and volatility was likely to surge.\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting Ian Chua and Hideyuki Sano; Editing by Toby Chopra) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-6-24T13:35:11.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160624ec6o01f39\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
