\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 596 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2016\par 14:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par U.K. Votes to Leave European Union \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Britons voted to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  in a startling rebuke that rattled financial markets and threatened to weaken a continent already strained by multiple crises. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par 'Brexit' Vote Wreaks Havoc in Markets \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Britain's vote to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  battered the British pound and sent stocks in Europe and Asia tumbling, pointing to a day of steep falls across the world's financial markets. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par U.K. Prime Minister Cameron to Resign \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 British Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 David Cameron\f28 \uc2 \f2  said he would step down after the U.K. voted to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  in a historic referendum. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOE to 'Take All Necessary Steps' Following 'Brexit' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of England\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it is working with other central banks to preserve the stability of the financial system as markets swooned following the U.K.'s decision to exit the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Germany's Merkel Calls for Calm and Unity After U.K. Vote to Leave EU \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 German Chancellor \f28 \uc2 \f2 Angela Merkel\f28 \uc2 \f2  called for calm and unity in the wake of the U.K. vote to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Fed Says Big Banks Cleared First Round of 'Stress Tests' \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The largest U.S. banks have significantly bolstered their defenses against a severe downturn, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2  said it has concluded, signaling that many will win regulators' approval next week to boost dividends to investors. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par European Banks Take Beating After 'Brexit' Vote \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 European banks took a beating in early trade, with \f28 \uc2 \f2 Barclays PLC\f28 \uc2 \f2  down nearly 30% at one point and other investment banks also suffering from widespread market uncertainty after the U.K. voted to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ECB\f28 \uc2 \f2  Ready to Provide Liquidity After Brexit Vote \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The \f28 \uc2 \f2 European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said it is closely monitoring financial markets in the wake of Britain's historic vote to exit the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 , and stands ready to provide additional liquidity in euros and foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Yen Surges as 'Brexit' Vote Sparks Search for Safety \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Japanese yen surged and other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were battered as voters in the U.K. upset market expectations and backed their nation leaving the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's Aso Renews \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Threat as Yen Soars \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister said he will take "firm action if necessary" to stem the yen's advance, reiterating his willingness to undertake direct \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as the U.K. vote to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2  sent the Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  soaring. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Brexit Won't Affect U.K.'s Membership of \f28 \uc2 \f2 NATO\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The head of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 North Atlantic Treaty Organization\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Britian's vote to leave the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  won't change the country's role in the military alliance. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Dutch Lawmaker Renews Pledge for EU Referendum \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dutch lawmaker Geert Wilders renewed his pledge to call a referendum on the Netherlands' membership of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  after Britain appeared to have voted in favor of a departure from the bloc. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Italy's Northern League To Launch Campaign For EU Referendum \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Italy's anti-immigrant and euroskeptic Northern League will start a petition calling for a law that allows a referendum on whether the country wants to exit the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 , its leader said. \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Fed's Kaplan Backs Away From Favoring Interest-Rate Increase in Summer \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve Bank of Dallas President \f28 \uc2 \f2 Robert Kaplan\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Thursday that he was backing away from his call earlier this year that he would favor raising rates this summer, citing a need to search for more evidence to justify a boost in borrowing costs.\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 24, 2016 08:31 ET (12:31 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160624ec6o0026k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
