\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Asia central banks, policymakers wade in to calm markets on Brexit vote\b0\par\par\uc2 841 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juni 2016\par 09:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Updating with comments from South Korean vice finance minister, economists)\par \par \uc2 By Saikat Chatterjee and Christine Kim\par \par \uc2 HONG KONG/SEOUL, June 24 (Reuters) - At least two Asian central banks were suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets on Friday, according to traders, as global financial markets went into a tailspin after Britain voted to leave the \uc2 European Union\uc2  in a historic vote.\par \par \uc2 Multiple traders said \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2  was thought to have sold dollars to curb the won's fall as the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dropped, while the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2  likely sold dollars through state-owned banks to prevent the rupee from falling further. [\par \par \uc2 An official at \uc2 the Bank of Korea\uc2  declined to comment, but South Korea's Vice Finance Minister Choi Sang-Mok said the government will make all efforts to minimize the impact from Brexit. "Regarding \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade, we will use all usable options to stabilize markets, including launching smoothing \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said.\par \par \uc2 A senior policymaker aware of the \uc2 Reserve Bank of India\uc2 's plans for Brexit-related market management said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is "prepared to deal with any volatility."\par \par \uc2 Separately, Japan's finance minister \uc2 Taro Aso\uc2  said he is carefully monitoring market developments and will respond as and when needed in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \uc2 A statement from the G7 group of leading industrial economies was expected on Friday. The question will be whether there is any coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ease monetary policy by global central banks, though room for maneuver is modest.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 The ECB\uc2  has few additional options left, yet it could announce more targeted purchases of peripheral sovereign bonds in the case investors start betting against the euro again," said Markus Schomer, chief economist at Pinebridge Investments.\par \par \uc2 The yen surging to its strongest levels against the dollar in two-and-a-half years, briefly breaking through the 100-yen-to-the-dollar level. Sterling suffered its biggest one-day fall of more than 9 percent against the dollar, hitting its lowest level in three decades.\par \par \uc2 Japanese stocks sank, pushing the Nikkei 225 index down more than 8 percent to its lowest since October 2014, and a similar decline in the Nikkei futures triggered circuit breakers.\par \par \uc2 Money markets were volatile. Fed fund futures effectively moved to pricing in a tiny U.S. rate cut from a rate increase in July.\par \par \uc2 Japan's Deputy Chief Cabinet Secretary Hiroshige Seko told reporters the government was worried about market moves, saying sudden shifts because of the British vote were undesirable.\par \par \uc2 The yen's strength due to its safe-haven status has been a frustration for Japanese authorities, who want a weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support exports and the economy. But they have been unable to garner support for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken it from other major economies, most notably the United States.\par \par \uc2 The 100-yen-per-dollar level has been seen as a pivotal point to test the patience of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary officials on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Morgan Stanley\uc2  expects the dollar to fall to 90 yen as investors seek the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  out as a relative safe haven, and a further 15-20 percent downside for European equities from current levels.\par \par \uc2 The Australian dollar, often sold off in times of heightened market stress, fell heavily against the dollar and the yen.\par \par \uc2 Traditional stress markers such as interbank dollar funding rates in Singapore and Hong Kong were broadly steady, but treasury bill and front end government bond yields fell.\par \par \uc2 "Because of this matter, we have made preparation in many aspects. We have reserved sufficient liquidity and we are able to handle in different situations," Hong Kong Financial Secretary John Tsang told reporters in the airport on Friday morning before he flew out to Beijing.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has asked banks to maintain ample cash conditions with them. No unscheduled monetary liquidity injection \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  have been taken so far, according to an HKMA spokeswoman.\par \par \uc2 The Singapore stock exchange played its part in trying to reduce volatility by raising margins on Nikkei futures traded on its exchange.\par \par \uc2 The People's Bank of China\uc2  injected 170 billion yuan ($25.9 billion) on Friday, taking the net injection for the week to 340 billion yuan, the biggest in two months. But that was seen more about averting a cash squeeze at the end of the half year next week, as has happened previously, rather than responding to the Brexit vote.\par \par \uc2 Still, the yuan fell to its weakest level against the U.S. dollar since January 2011 while its offshore counterpart slipped to its weakest level in more than four months.\par \par \uc2 The Philippines' \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday it was closely monitoring the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and remains prepared to act to ensure orderly transactions and smooth volatility. (Additional reporting by Donny Kwok, Christine Kim in SEOUL, Jianxin Lu and Nathaniel Taplin in SHANGHAI, Neha Dasgipta in NEW DELHI and Saeed Azhar in SINGAPORE; Writing by \uc2 John Mair\uc2 ; Editing by Martin Howell) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-6-24T08:19:48.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160624ec6o00wfc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
