\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Top Economic Stories of the Day\b0\par\par\uc2 1,033 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2016\par 03:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ Officials Cite Weak Econ, Wage Growth for April Price Forecast Cut \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials cut price forecasts at their April meeting because of weakness in economic growth and wage increases, rather than cheaper oil, an indication that they recognized problems in their rosy inflation scenario. (published 0047 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Australia Forecasts 2.5% Fall in Annual Farm Export Earnings \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Earnings from Australian farm exports look set to dip this financial year due an anticipated lower world prices for grains and a drop in domestic beef supplies, a government report released Tuesday said. (published 0039 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Fed's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Neel Kashkari\f28 \uc2 \f2   Says He Had Trouble Getting a Mortgage \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 It turns out being a regional Federal Reserve president doesn't make it any easier to be a bank customer. (published 0028 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Brazil Treasury Offers Relief to Indebted State Governments \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Brazil's Finance Ministry\f28 \uc2 \f2  cut a deal with financially strapped state governments on Monday to alleviate high debt-service costs that have forced them to slash spending on critical public services such as policing, education and health care. (published 2315 GMT Monday) \f28 \par \par \par \par \uc2 \f2 20 Jun 2016 23:02 ET \par News Highlights: Top Economic Stories of the Day\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ April Minutes: Weakening Inflation Not Due to Oil Prices -- Update \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials recognized in April that more fundamental problems than cheaper oil were weakening inflation, but they couldn't agree on how they might counter mounting risks to their rosy price scenario. (published 0235 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Plays Cautious On Rates \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  indicated Tuesday it will remain cautious for now, stopping short of introducing a clear bias to further lower interest rates in minutes of its June 7 policy meeting. (published 0133 GMT) \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Finance Minister: Won't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Over Yen 'Easily' \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister said Tuesday the government wouldn't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets "easily," in a sharp shift in rhetoric suggesting that global criticism may have made Tokyo less eager to undertake steps to weaken the yen. (published 0216 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par BOJ Officials Cite Weak Econ, Wage Growth for April Price Forecast Cut \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials cut price forecasts at their April meeting because of weakness in economic growth and wage increases, rather than cheaper oil, an indication that they recognized problems in their rosy inflation scenario. (published 0047 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Australia Forecasts 2.5% Fall in Annual Farm Export Earnings \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Earnings from Australian farm exports look set to dip this financial year due an anticipated lower world prices for grains and a drop in domestic beef supplies, a government report released Tuesday said. (published 003