\par\par \b \uc2 News Highlights: Economic Stories Of The Day\b0\par\par\uc2 348 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2016\par 12:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 European Stocks Steady After Sharp Gains\par \par \uc2 European stocks were little changed a day after signs that the U.K. may vote to remain in the \uc2 European Union\uc2  spurred their greatest one-day gain since August.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Aso Says Won't \b \highlight22\uc2 Intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  Over Yen 'Easily'\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's finance minister said Tuesday the government wouldn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets "easily," a sharp shift in rhetoric suggesting that global criticism may have made Tokyo less eager to undertake steps to weaken the yen.\par \par \uc2 German Court Rejects Legal Challenge to ECB Bond-Buying\par \par \uc2 Germany's top court has ruled that an unlimited bond-buying program created by the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the height of Europe's debt crisis complies with German law, ending a yearslong legal challenge.\par \par \uc2 Belgian Premier Says 'Situation is Under Control' After Terror Alert\par \par \uc2 Charles Michel\uc2  met with senior security officials Tuesday morning after a suspect was arrested at the City2 shopping centre.\par \par \uc2 Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Plays Cautious on Rates\par \par \uc2 Australia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  indicated it will remain cautious for now, stopping short of introducing a clear bias to further lower interest rates in minutes of its June 7 policy meeting, released Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Naira Plunges After Nigeria Ends Dollar Peg\par \par \uc2 Nigeria's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plummeted more than 40% against the dollar on Monday, the latest sign that low crude prices continue to disrupt the economies of some major oil-producing nations.\par \par \uc2 Iraq Refugees Languish Outside Fallujah\par \par \uc2 As government forces fight to take the city back from Islamic State militants, thousands of residents have fled to camps.\par \par \uc2 Trump Severs Ties With Campaign Aide \uc2 Corey Lewandowski\par \par \uc2 Presumptive Republican presidential nominee \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has severed ties with campaign manager \uc2 Corey Lewandowski\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ECB Corporate Bond-Buying Was $2.26 Billion Last Week\par \par \uc2 The ECB\uc2  kept up an aggressive pace of corporate bond-buying last week putting it on track to buy around $9 billion a month in its new stimulus program that policy makers hope will help drive up inflation.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 21, 2016 06:00 ET (10:00 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160621ec6l000rl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
