\par\par \b \uc2 Dow Jones Asia-Pacific Top Stories Sked for June 21\b0\par\par\uc2 865 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2016\par 08:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Following are the top Asian-Pacific stories featured on Dow Jones Newswires as of 0600 GMT. Not all stories appear on all wires.\par \par \uc2 MACRO/\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 /FIXED INCOME: \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Thailand's Automotive Industry Sees Further Recovery in May \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's automotive industry continued its slow recovery in May as general business environment picked up from the previous month, according to the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federation of Thai Industries\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0419 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Thai Industrial Sentiment Recovers in May \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Thailand's industrial sentiment rebounded in May due to eased worries about the impact of drought and an improved business environment for certain sectors, the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federation of Thai Industries\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday. (published 0341 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ April Minutes: Weakening Inflation Not Due to Oil Prices -- Update \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials recognized in April that more fundamental problems than cheaper oil were weakening inflation, but they couldn't agree on how they might counter mounting risks to their rosy price scenario. (published 0235 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Plays Cautious On Rates \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Australia's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  indicated Tuesday it will remain cautious for now, stopping short of introducing a clear bias to further lower interest rates in minutes of its June 7 policy meeting. (published 0133 GMT) \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Finance Minister: Won't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Over Yen 'Easily' \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's finance minister said Tuesday the government wouldn't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets "easily," in a sharp shift in rhetoric suggesting that global criticism may have made Tokyo less eager to undertake steps to weaken the yen. (published 0216 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par BOJ Officials Cite Weak Econ, Wage Growth for April Price Forecast Cut \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  officials cut price forecasts at their April meeting because of weakness in economic growth and wage increases, rather than cheaper oil, an indication that they recognized problems in their rosy inflation scenario. (published 0047 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Australia Forecasts 2.5% Fall in Annual Farm Export Earnings \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Earnings from Australian farm exports look set to dip this financial year due an anticipated lower world prices for grains and a drop in domestic beef supplies, a government report released Tuesday said. (published 0039 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Wuxi Construction & Development Investment Raises US$300 Mln via USD Bond Offering -- Term Sheet \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wuxi Construction & Development Investment Co., a local-government financial vehicle owned by the Wuxi municipal government in China's Jiangsu province, raised US$300 million via a U.S. dollar-denominated bond offering for general corporate purposes and working capital, according to a term sheet seen Tuesday by The Wall Street Journal. (published 0111 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EQUITIES: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Malaysia's Top Glove Looks to Expand; Expects Secondary Listing in Singapore Late June \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Malaysia's \f28 \uc2 \f2 Top Glove Corp. Bhd\f28 \uc2 \f2 ., the world largest rubber-glove maker by volume, targets to expand by acquiring at least one peer before the end of the year, Chairman \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lim Wee Chai\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday. (published 0457 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par Rosneft in Deal to Sell Crude Oil to \f28 \uc2 \f2 PetroVietnam\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Russian oil firm Rosneft has signed a deal to sell crude oil to the trading arm of Vietnam's state-run oil firm \f28 \uc2 \f2 PetroVietnam\f28 \uc2 \f2 , \f28 \uc2 \f2 PetroVietnam\f28 \uc2 \f2  said Tuesday. (published 0408 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Frasers Logistics & Industrial Trust\f28 \uc2 \f2  Opens 1.7% Higher on Debut \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Frasers Logistics & Industrial Trust\f28 \uc2 \f2 , owned by Thai millionaire \f28 \uc2 \f2 Charoen Sirivadhanabhakdi\f28 \uc2 \f2 , opened 1.7% higher on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Singapore Exchange\f28 \uc2 \f2  in its debut. (published 0124 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nissan\f28 \uc2 \f2 : Began Legal Proceedings Monday Vs Brexit "Leave" Campaign on Use of Nissan Logo \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Nissan Motor Co\f28 \uc2 \f2 . said Tuesday that it began legal proceedings Monday against a group that supports the U.K. leaving the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  for its use of the Japanese car maker's logo. (published 0118 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Modern Land (China) to Buy a Plot of Land in Nanjing \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Modern Land Co. will buy a plot of land in Nanjing, China, for a total of 1.02 billion yuan . (published 0040 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ta Yang Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  to Buy Hotel Properties for CNY357.5 Million \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Ta Yang Group Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . agreed to buy hotel properties in the southern Chinese resort city of Sanya for 357.5 million yuan, as the Hong Kong-listed manufacturer seeks to diversify. (published 0020 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NWS Holdings\f28 \uc2 \f2  to Sell NWS Kwai Chung Logistics Center For HK$3.75 Billion \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NWS Holdings Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . has agreed to sell an investment property to a unit of \f28 \uc2 \f2 China Resources Enterprise Ltd\f28 \uc2 \f2 . for 3.75 billion Hong Kong dollars . (published 0007 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par China-Based Hacking Incidents See Dip, Cybersecurity Experts Say \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Chinese hacking of corporate and government networks in the U.S. and other countries appears to be declining, according to computer-security experts at companies hired to investigate these breaches. (published 0001 GMT) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Asian Shares Mostly Higher on Relief Over 'Brexit' Polls \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Shares in Asia broadly rose Tuesday as investors bet that the U.K. would vote to remain in the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0358 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 ENERGY/COMMODITIES: \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Oil Prices Pare Gains; Focus on Brexit and U.S. Oil Data \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Crude prices broke a two-day gain in early Asian trade Tuesday, as market players turn their attention back to the persistent overhang of oil on reduced odds of U.K. leaving the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (published 0321 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 21, 2016 02:18 ET (06:18 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160621ec6l0009i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
