\par\par \b \uc2 Thailand's SET Flirts With Gains on Brexit Poll -- Brexit Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,446 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Juni 2016\par 12:09\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 1009 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Thailand's SET ends up 0.1% at 1421.99 flirting with gains along with other Asian markets after a poll showed that Britain may be less likely to leave the \uc2 European Union\uc2  than previously thought. Oil and energy companies trend higher, as oil prices also gain. Thai Oil (TOP.TH), for example, ends up 0.4%, while \uc2 PTT Exploration & Production\uc2  (PTTEP.TH) ends up 2.8% after publishing its first quarter results analysis. \uc2 Glow Energy\uc2  (GLOW.TH) is the exception, down 1.8%, while TMB Bank (TMB.TH) falls 1.8%. (jake.watts@wsj.com; Twitter: @jmwatts_) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 1006 GMT Issues from supranational and sovereign agencies, such as the \uc2 European Financial Stability Facility\uc2  and the \uc2 European Investment Bank\uc2 , have become substantially cheaper compared with \uc2 German government\uc2  bonds following recent market moves, says \uc2 Nordea\uc2 . This is especially the case in maturities beyond the 10-year mark, analyst Uffe Kalmar Hansen says. The widening SSA-bund gap shows investors have yet another reason to focus on the U.K. referendum on \uc2 EU\uc2  membership on June 23, as a 'Remain' outcome will "very likely" lead to SSA outperformance versus bunds. (tasos.vossos@wsj.com, @tasosvos) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 1003 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The \f28 \uc2 \f2 International Monetary Fund\f28 \uc2 \f2  is giving Japan the cold shoulder over the issue of whether action to stem the yen's rise is warranted, underscoring lack of global support for \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Tokyo. "\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has a set of understandings with its partner countries in the \f28 \uc2 \f2 G-7\f28 \uc2 \f2  and the G-20, with respect to exchange rate policy," IMF Deputy Managing Director \f28 \uc2 \f2 David Lipton\f28 \uc2 \f2 , who is in Tokyo for annual policy dialogues, says in an interview Monday. "Those understandings are for Japan to sort out with those partners." The remarks by \f28 \uc2 \f2 IMF\f28 \uc2 \f2 's No. 2 official come in contrast to what he said in the summer of 2012, when he noted that, if market forces "lead to disruptive flows, short-term smoothing is something that we would understand." The difference suggests that the rest of the world views the yen as still being at levels with which Japan's exporters can live with. The USD/JPY is currently at around Y104.50, compared with around Y80.00 in June 2012. (takashi.nakamichi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JFN \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0959 GMT Slovakia's EUR388 million government bond sale at its monthly auction Monday heralds the beginning of a summer bond sale pause as the Central European sovereign's next bond auction is scheduled for Sept. 19. Ardal, the Slovak debt agency, didn't conduct bond auctions in the July and August months of 2015 and 2014 either. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0954 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The FTSE \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bursa Malaysia\f28 \uc2 \f2  Index ends Monday higher alongside positive Asian markets driven by expectations that the U.K. will remain in the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  at the end of this week, after all. The better showing also comes after Malaysia's ruling government secured a strong victory at two special elections on Saturday, thanks in part to a divided opposition. Malaysia's 30-stocks benchmark index closes 0.62% higher at 1,634.23 points at a one-week high, mainly driven by real estate investment trust KLCC Property (5235SS.KU) and lender CIMB (1023.KU). Among the losers in the index are oil and gas \f28 \uc2 \f2 SapuraKencana Petroleum\f28 \uc2 \f2  (5218.KU) and lender \f28 \uc2 \f2 Hong Leong Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2  (5819.KU). (yantoultra.ngui@wsj.com; Twitter: @yantoultra) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0951 GMT After Sunday's municipal elections, economist \f28 \uc2 \f2 Lorenzo Codogno\f28 \uc2 \f2  says Italy's political scene has become a tri-party system in which the anti-establishment 5-Star Movement is taking the lead as the major opposition party. Mr. Codogno, a former senior official at the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Italian economy ministry\f28 \uc2 \f2 , adds that given the internal division of the center-right, the 5-Star Movement will be the leading opposition party to Prime Minister \f28 \uc2 \f2 Matteo Renzi\f28 \uc2 \f2 's PD at the next parliamentary election expected in early 2018. It will be key to see whether 5-Star Movement politicians become more pragmatic and moderate as this may shift the balance of votes in their favor. (liam.moloney@dowjones.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0944 GMT Swedish construction company NCC has seen 2Q orders rising 180% year-on-year so far this quarter. This "boom," as Swedbank calls it, is positive news for NCC spreads; it reinforces the bank's overweight on NCC medium-term notes and its view that NCC has a strong underlying business. Swedbank upgraded its shadow rating on NCC by two notches to BBB+ on Friday. However, it points out that the orders' concentration to Sweden is somewhat negative. (tasos.vossos@wsj.com, @tasosvos) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0944 GMT \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2  advises buying EUR/CZK, targeting 28.00 and a stop at 27.00, compared with 27.06 currently. EUR/CZK moves within a tight range because of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Czech National Bank\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to maintain a 27.00 floor, leaving it less vulnerable to sharp moves following the U.K.'s referendum on \f28 \uc2 \f2 EU\f28 \uc2 \f2  membership on Thursday. Brexit concerns last week caused central and eastern European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to fall against the euro. The Czech koruna also fell, albeit modestly, and it would drop further on a Brexit vote. On a remain vote, however, EUR/CZK downside would be limited to 27. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Morgan Stanley\f28 \uc2 \f2  says this is a "tactical trade", which it would "look to exit in a Remain scenario with a small loss." (jessica.fleetham@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0942 GMT \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Telekom\f28 \uc2 \f2  is reportedly considering a bid for internet domain registry \f28 \uc2 \f2 Host Europe Group\f28 \uc2 \f2  and a deal could prove to be a credit-negative event, says \f28 \uc2 \f2 UniCredit\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Analyst Stephan Haber keeps the marketweight recommendation on the issuer, as the transaction and its impact are still vague. However, the telecom group's credit metrics look "stretched" and an acquisition, even a medium-sized one, could have negative implications. Host Europe could be worth around EUR1.7 billion, Mr. Haber points out. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Deutsche Telekom\f28 \uc2 \f2  declines to comment. (tasos.vossos@wsj.com, @tasosvos) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Contact us in London. +44-20-7842-9464 \par markettalk@wsj.com \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0938 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] A Japanese college student on Monday asked Bank of Japan Governor Haruhiko Kuroda, who has a history of shocking the markets with his surprise easing decisions, if he would ever hint at policy moves, such that markets might be able to prepare for his moves. The BOJ chief answered it was not the job of a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to influence the ways that markets react to policies--so such a signalling would be unproductive. Nevertheless, he did use the meeting to flag the direction of his policies--Kuroda repeated his pledge to take additional easing "without hesitation" if necessary. (megumi.fujikawa@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0931 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The FTSE Straits Times Index ends Monday up 1.4% at 2800.87, boosted by offshore marine companies and financials after a new poll on Britain's \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  referendum showed increased support for remaining within the bloc. The STI gains in line with--or more than--other Asian markets, with sold-down stocks typically among the better performers despite a lack of much corporate news. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Golden Agri-Resources\f28 \uc2 \f2  (E5H.SG) and \f28 \uc2 \f2 SembCorp Industries\f28 \uc2 \f2  (U96.SG) rise 5.8% and 3.3%, respectively, while \f28 \uc2 \f2 Oversea-Chinese Banking Corp\f28 \uc2 \f2 . (O39.SG) and DBS (D05.SG) end up 2.4% and 2.2%, respectively. Off-index, Noble Group (N21.SG) extends its 13-year low with another 6.5% loss. (jake.watts@wsj.com; Twitter: @jmwatts_) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0928 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Devesh Ashra and Conan Tam were named \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of America Merrill Lynch\f28 \uc2 \f2 's co-heads of Asia Pacific debt solutions, according to an internal memo sent Monday viewed by The Wall Street Journal. In these newly created roles, they will have responsibility across debt capital markets, leveraged finance and syndicated loans. Ashra previously was head of Asia DCM syndicate at the Wall Street investment bank, while Tam was head of greater China debt capital markets. BAML declined to comment on the new appointments. (carol.chan@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 20, 2016 06:09 ET (10:09 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160620ec6k00105\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
