\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-Hints of  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  as central banks debate Brexit response\b0\par\par\uc2 732 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 2016\par 08:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Repeats Thursday item without changes)\par \par \uc2 By Patrick Graham and Anirban Nag\par \par \uc2 LONDON, June 16 (Reuters) - Warnings from officials in Japan and Switzerland on Thursday left financial markets wondering about what central banks are planning behind the scenes if Britain votes to leave the \uc2 European Union\uc2  next week.\par \par \uc2 It is five years since major monetary authorities waded in to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets in a concerted push to quell gains for the yen after a shattering earthquake in Japan.\par \par \uc2 Such coordinated action in the era of floating exchange rates is rare, and central banks have so far restricted themselves to promises to provide any funding banks might need in the event of a stormy aftermath to next Thursday's referendum.\par \par \uc2 Officials told Reuters earlier this week the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would pledge to backstop markets in tandem with the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  after a vote to leave.\par \par \uc2 But a raft of official policy statements following four major \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  meetings this week -- and amid evidence that momentum within the British electorate is shifting towards the Brexit camp -- offered hints that policymakers are considering whether they will need to do more.\par \par \uc2 "Sharp fluctuations could occur in the \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, with the pound depreciating massively amid low liquidity. This could prompt the central banks of the developed countries to conduct joint \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Antje Praefcke, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2  in Frankfurt.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Swiss National Bank\uc2  said outright it would be active on the franc and would take steps to counter any Brexit fallout. Chairman \uc2 Thomas Jordan\uc2  added central banks were holding intense exchanges on market developments.\par \par \uc2 "We have a global view, we follow markets on a 24-hour basis," SNB governing board member \uc2 Andrea Maechler\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the subject of intense speculation since January over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the yen, refrained from offering additional monetary stimulus on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 That sent the yen, a safe-haven during times of financial market stress, to a two-year high, up three percent against sterling.\par \par \uc2 Government spokesman \uc2 Yoshihide Suga\uc2  expressed concern about the yen's rise and said Japan would respond if needed.\par \par \uc2 "The SNB and potentially the \uc2 Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would want to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and drive down the value of their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Yujiro Goto, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Nomura in London.\par \par \uc2 "It is pretty clear, especially with the SNB... that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be the first line of defence for them."\par \par \uc2 FRANC LESSONS\par \par \uc2 Leading figures on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market are nervous that a "Leave" vote might spawn the kind of gaps in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market pricing that provoked chaos when the SNB lifted its cap on the franc in January 2015.\par \par \uc2 Traders and analysts say liquidity conditions during Asian trade, when the referendum results will start to trickle in, are likely to be thin and bid/offer spreads are likely to widen.\par \par \uc2 Some say they have told the \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  that if there are large gaps it should be prepared to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  steadily to prevent huge swings in the market as banks and investors seek to establish a new price for sterling.\par \par \uc2 In the case of the franc, the overshooting of rates played a role in bankrupting some retail brokerages and dozens of their clients, while major banks and hedge funds faced hundreds of millions in losses.\par \par \uc2 Strategists in London are loath to discuss the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  publicly but many have predicted double-digit falls in sterling if Britain votes to leave.\par \par \uc2 The main objective of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  "would be to dampen excessive near-term fluctuations and prevent things from getting worse," \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 's Praefcke said.\par \par \uc2 The mechanics would involve the swap lines banks opened up to each other to ensure \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were available amid vanishing liquidity during the global financial crises of 2008.\par \par \uc2 At that point, the \uc2 Reserve Bank of Australia\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in New York as well as Sydney to provide Australian dollar liquidity after bid/offer spreads widened, making trading close to impossible.\par \par \uc2 The RBA was clear then that it was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  not with any level in mind but to smooth out liquidity conditions.\par \par \uc2 ""There are some examples in the past when central banks have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in volatile markets," said \uc2 HSBC\uc2  strategist Dominic Bunning. "Obviously we are considering what may or may not happen." (Writing by Patrick Graham; editing by John Stonestreet)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-6-20T06:22:01.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160617ec6h00hqx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
