\par\par \b \uc2 ASIA MARKETS: Japan Stocks Recover After A Mess Of A Week\b0\par\par\uc2 By Chao Deng   \par \uc2 557 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 2016\par 11:36\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 Nikkei drops 6% for the week\par \par \uc2 Stocks in Japan rose from a four-month low and led most Asian markets higher on Friday, although worries about the upcoming U.K. vote on \uc2 European Union\uc2  membership left the region's markets badly bruised for the week.\par \par \uc2 The Nikkei Stock Average closed up 1.1%, while the Hang Seng Index was up 0.7% and the Shanghai Composite Index rose 0.4%. Australia's S&P \uc2 ASX\uc2  200 finished up 0.3%.\par \par \uc2 The Nikkei finished the week off 6%, marking its worst weekly performance since the week ended Feb. 12. Hong Kong lost more than 4%, while the Shanghai finished down 1.4% for the week.\par \par \uc2 Some investors appear willing to buy shares after several days of declines, which made for a resilient market Friday.\par \par \uc2 A recovery began overnight, as U.S. stocks climbed and snapped a five-session streak of declines. The market started the day lower after the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  dashed hopes for additional monetary easing, amid concerns about the impact of a coming U.K. vote on whether to remain in the \uc2 EU\uc2 . But official campaigning ahead of the referendum was halted ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.marketwatch.com/story/brexit-debate-thrown-into-limbo-after-death-of-uk-lawmaker-jo-cox-2016-06-17"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.marketwatch.com/story/brexit-debate-thrown-into-limbo-after-death-of-uk-lawmaker-jo-cox-2016-06-17}}}\uc2 ) Thursday after an attacker killed a lawmaker from the U.K.'s Labour Party ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.marketwatch.com/story/british-labour-party-lawmaker-attacked-man-arrested-2016-06-16"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.marketwatch.com/story/british-labour-party-lawmaker-attacked-man-arrested-2016-06-16}}}\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 In Asia, analysts pointed to the closeness of polls tracking the \uc2 EU\uc2  membership vote and the possibility of a market rebound should the U.K. choose to remain in the bloc when it votes on June 23.\par \par \uc2 "I still lean to a 'remain' outcome," said Shane Oliver, a Sydney-based investment strategist at AMP Capital. In that case, "recent market moves should reverse with the British pound and Eurozone shares are likely to bounce particularly sharply."\par \par \uc2 In Japan, shares closed Thursday at their second-lowest point this year, but were recovering on Friday as the Japanese yen reversed its strengthening trend.\par \par \uc2 The yen recently weakened by 0.3% against the U.S. dollar to 104.20 yen per dollar during Asia hours Friday.\par \par \uc2 Investors are watching the yen closely--the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded at Yen103.58 during Asia hours Thursday--and many analysts think that strengthening from that level raises the likelihood that the finance ministry will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  ({\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.wsj.com/articles/u-s-and-japan-heading-for-standoff-on-yen-devaluation-1463678715"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.wsj.com/articles/u-s-and-\b  \highlight22japan\b0 \highlight22 -heading-for-standoff-on-yen-devaluation-1463678715}}}\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 Now trading near a two-year high, the stronger yen has become a major headache for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  because it restrains efforts to stoke inflation and spark growth, while making Japanese exports less competitive abroad.\par \par \uc2 "It might have made sense for them to hold off," Nicholas Ferres, portfolio manager for global asset allocation at Eastspring Investments, said of the BOJ's announcement to hold off on further easing Thursday afternoon. "They have a few bullets left in the barrel or ammunition if they need to use it over coming weeks."\par \par \uc2 The Nikkei is off about 18% since the beginning of the year, but Ferres said his team is overweight on Japanese equities.\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 June 17, 2016 05:36 ET (09:36 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160617ec6h000vx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
