\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  May  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  When Yen Crosses 105 Threshold -- Barron's Blog\b0\par\par\uc2 By Shuli Ren   \par \uc2 224 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 2016\par 04:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 When the yen has crossed the 105 per dollar threshold, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, warns Citi Research.\par \par \uc2 Yesterday, the yen soared past 104 per dollar after the \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  decided to keep its monetary policies unchanged. This morning, Finance Minister \uc2 Taro Aso\uc2  told reporters that Japan would " act more firmly than before if necessary" against rapid yen movements.\par \par \uc2 Japan may be able to convince its \uc2 G-7\uc2  allies that it is not a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulator if it uses purchasing-power parity fair valuation. \uc2 OECD\uc2  puts yen PPP at 106.04 per dollar, the \uc2 World Bank\uc2  puts it at 105.27 per dollar, and the \uc2 IMF\uc2  puts it at 103.22 per dollar, noted Citi. So yes, when yen dips below the 105 threshold, Japan can legitimately claim it is just helping the invisible hand to re-balance faster.\par \par \uc2 This morning, the yen retreated 0.2% to 104.56. The Nikkei 225 jumped 1.6%. Overnight, the \uc2 iShares MSCI Japan ETF\uc2  (EWJ) fell 0.4%, but the \uc2 WisdomTree Japan Hedged Equity Fund\uc2  (DXJ) tumbled 2.4%. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  More at Barron's Asia Stocks to Watch blog, \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://blogs.barrons.com/asiastocks/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://blogs.barrons.com/asiastocks/}}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \