\par\par \b \uc2 EUR/USD Jumps Out of Gutter on Likely Reduced Odds of Brexit -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,848 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juni 2016\par 04:20\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 0220 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The EUR/USD has nullified chances of a bearish technical breakdown, with its overnight jump out of the Bollinger downtrend channel and return inside the Ichimoku Cloud support zone. The base of the Cloud now props the pair up at 1.1217, while the entrance of the downtrend channel at 1.1150 would be the next chart floor. The euro rebounded, together with the pound, as the odds of a 'Brexit' may have fallen after the alleged murder of a U.K. lawmaker, who was campaigning for Britain to remain in the \uc2 European Union\uc2 . Hopes for the status quo to remain in the \uc2 EU\uc2  also fuelled an overnight rally on Wall Street and triggered a sharp pullback in haven gold prices. The EUR/USD may rise toward the 1.1319 technical resistance, where the Bollinger uptrend channel begins, as punters bet that the next poll might show a shift toward the 'Bremain' camp. The EUR/USD is now at 1.1265 from its Thursday closing of 1.1223. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JFN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 0220 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] NZD/USD Intraday: Key resistance at 0.7085. The pair failed to break above its horizontal resistance and overlap at 0.7085 after having tested for at least two times yesterday. Meanwhile, a bearish cross has been identified between the 20-period and 50-period moving averages, which should call for further decline. To conclude, as long as 0.7085 is not surpassed, look for a new pullback to 0.7030 and then to 0.7005. Alternative scenario, above 0.7085, expect further upside with 0.7120 & 0.7150 as targets. [This piece contains the opinions of Trading Central and does not constitute personalized investment advice or form part of any invitation or inducement to buy or sell any security. The author has been prohibited by Trading Central from purchasing or otherwise directly or indirectly acquiring any direct or indirect beneficial ownership of any instruments or markets for which Trading Central or its affiliates issues recommendations. To read more, visit bit.ly/1MehCU9] (analysts@tradingcentral.com) \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0213 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Could the yen break below 100 to one U.S. dollar? After the yen briefly strengthened past 104 this week, some analysts and traders are already entertaining the possibility of a return to a level to 100 or below. Such a move would further support the case that Abenomics have failed to boost Japan's economy, as a strong yen pressures earnings at large Japanese exporters. For now, pressure has eased off the yen to strengthen more ahead of the 'Brexit' vote next week, as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was recently trading around 104.6190 per dollar. Traders are warily watching the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's repeated rhetoric about their willingness to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and introduce additional easing measures if necessary. "If trust in the BOJ evaporates, all hell will break loose," said Mingze Wu, head of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading at INTL FCStone's Global Payments Division in Singapore. But "if the market is confident in easing, and trusts in Abenomics, then it [the yen] won't break 100." (dominique.fong@wsj.com; \f28 \uc2 \f2 Twitter\f28 \uc2 \f2 : @dominiquefong) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JFN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0207 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The yen's strength against the U.S. dollar to 103.20 may spark \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  jitters, says IG Securities' Junichi Ishikawa in a morning note. The level is a break-even point for Japanese exporters, according to a survey by the Cabinet Office, and yen strength above this point will likely heighten volatility of the USD/JPY trade, says Ishikawa. On the flip side, the focus for now is on whether the dollar finds the Y105-line as a resistance. But even if the dollar successfully breaks above the Y105 mark, the greenback may again weaken below the line, as long as the dollar fails to breach the USD/JPY 5-day moving average of 105.40. (hiroyuki.kachi@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: JFN \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0205 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] GBP/USD Intraday: Turning up. The pair is turning up and is expected to post further rebound. Besides, both the 20-period and 50-period moving averages are heading upward, calling for further upside. Last but not least, the relative strength index is still positive above its neutrality area at 50. To sum up, as long as 1.4190 is not broken, we are positive and expect a bounce to 1.4295 and 1.4325. Alternatively, only a break below the key support at 1.4190 would confirm a negative view, and call for a new drop toward 1.4140 as likely. [This piece contains the opinions of Trading Central and does not constitute personalized investment advice or form part of any invitation or inducement to buy or sell any security. The author has been prohibited by Trading Central from purchasing or otherwise directly or indirectly acquiring any direct or indirect beneficial ownership of any instruments or markets for which Trading Central or its affiliates issues recommendations. To read more, visit bit.ly/1MehCU9] (analysts@tradingcentral.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0154 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Yuzhou Properties\f28 \uc2 \f2  (1628.HK) said late Thursday that it has issued 2 billion yuan of onshore bonds via its mainland subsidiary. The three-year bonds carry a coupon of 6.28%. Research firm Lucror Analytics says the Chinese property developer has been gradually replacing high-cost foreign-\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bonds with low-cost onshore yuan bonds. Lucror believes it is likely that Yuzhou will repurchase its US$300 million, 8.75% dollar bonds due 2018 when the bonds are callable in the coming October given their high cost. Lucror maintains a hold recommendation on the 2018 bonds. (carol.chan@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0150 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] USD/CHF Intraday: Bullish bias above 0.9620. The pair reversed up, and remains bullish above its horizontal support at 0.9620. Further upsides are likely to challenge the nearest resistance at 0.9685. Additionally, a bullish cross has been identified between the 20-period and 50-period moving averages. In addition, the relative strength index lacks downward momentum. Hence, as long as 0.9620 holds on the downside, the intraday outlook stays positive with targets at 0.9685 & 0.9705 in extension. Alternatively, below 0.9620, expect a pullback to 0.9590 & 0.9570 as targets. [This piece contains the opinions of Trading Central and does not constitute personalized investment advice or form part of any invitation or inducement to buy or sell any security. The author has been prohibited by Trading Central from purchasing or otherwise directly or indirectly acquiring any direct or indirect beneficial ownership of any instruments or markets for which Trading Central or its affiliates issues recommendations. To read more, visit bit.ly/1MehCU9] (analysts@tradingcentral.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0142 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Nicholas Ferres, portfolio manager for global asset allocation at Eastspring Investments, says the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 's negative interest rates are poor policy that may be limiting credit creation. He says policy steps that damage bank profits would likely discourage banks from lending more, which is the opposite of the policy goal. "What you're trying to do is to create credit growth, in other words, get the banks to lend. If you're damaging, whether directly or indirectly, their profits, you're not helping. You're actually making the problem worse," he says. The BOJ decided to introduce the negative interest rate policy in January, drawing criticism from some financial industry officials. (kosaku.narioka@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0137 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] Nicholas Ferres, portfolio manager for global asset allocation at Eastspring Investments, says the yen is undervalued from real effective exchange rate basis and improvement in Japan's trade positions also point to a higher yen. The yen has gained some 15% so far this year. In the longer-run, however, Ferres says the outlook is murkier, particularly if the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  ends up taking extraordinary steps to address Japan's fiscal problems. "If the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  eventually does outright monetization, that may be problematic for the yen in the long run," he says. The USD/JPY is at 104.72.(kosaku.narioka@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: KLH \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0136 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 The People's Bank of China\f28 \uc2 \f2  set Friday's yuan mid-point at 6.5795 versus Thursday's 6.5739, representing a 0.1% weakening of the yuan against the U.S. dollar. The U.S. dollar index crept up overnight, influencing the USD/CNY parity rate today. The greenback has subsided since, with slimmer odds of a "Brexit" occurring, which ought to result in a lower USD/CNY fixing on Monday. The yuan has been whipsawing of late, in the wake of the \f28 \uc2 \f2 MSCI\f28 \uc2 \f2  decision to keep Chinese shares out of its Emerging Markets index for now. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's volatility may continue, though the \f28 \uc2 \f2 MSCI\f28 \uc2 \f2  effect has faded, due to wild gyrations of the Japanese yen. The yen acts as a beacon for many Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and on Thursday rallied to a 22-month peak when the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2  kept policy unchanged. The yen is now weakening, on fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . USD/CNY is now at 6.5848 from its official close of 6.5840 on Thursday. (ewen.chew@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: MNG \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0132 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] The \f28 \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan\f28 \uc2 \f2 's policy inertia Thursday made some sense given several near-term risk events, but it also raised questions about its commitment to its inflation goal, says Nicholas Ferres, portfolio manager for global asset allocation at Eastspring Investments. "It might have made a sense for them to hold off...so that they have a few bullets left in the barrel or ammunition if they need to use it over coming weeks." Ferres listed the U.K. referendum on the \f28 \uc2 \f2 European Union\f28 \uc2 \f2  membership next week, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Japan's upper house\f28 \uc2 \f2  election, and the \f28 \uc2 \f2 Federal Reserve\f28 \uc2 \f2 's meeting in July among possible risk events. "That said, the bank is missing its inflation target and it is losing some credibility." (kosaku.narioka@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor JSM \par  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 16 Jun 2016 22:20 ET \par EUR/USD Jumps Out of Gutter on Likely Reduced -2-\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 0130 GMT [\f28 \uc2 \f2 Dow Jones\f28 \uc2 \f2 ] \f28 \uc2 \f2 Goldman Sachs\f28 \uc2 \f2  lines up the evidence that China is still backing up domestic firms in danger of default, unwilling to let market forces play their full role: For seven out of the 18 notable defaults in the Chinese onshore corporate bond market, investors have received on par recovery payments, according to the firm's estimates. That includes Bohai Steel, which avoided a technical default by making a deposit before a one-month grace period was due. The remaining 11 issuers have total bonds outstanding of 34.8 billion yuan, or 0.2% of the 15 trillion yuan of domestic corporate bonds outstanding as of the end of 2015. (chao.deng@wsj.com) \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Editor: TFD \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 June 16, 2016 22:20 ET (02:20 GMT)\f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160617ec6h0007g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
