\par\par \b \uc2 Bank of Japan Gov Kuroda Again Signals Stance Against Higher Yen\b0\par\par\uc2 By Takashi Nakamichi   \par \uc2 248 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 2016\par 07:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones Newswires Chinese (English)\par \uc2 RTNW\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 TOKYO--Bank of Japan Gov. Haruhiko Kuroda suggested Wednesday that sharp yen rises could spur the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to action, reflecting heightened concerns among Tokyo policy makers about a potential resurgence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "Generally speaking, it is desirable that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates move stably in reflection of economic and financial fundamentals, but things don't necessarily work that way," Mr. Kuroda, formerly a senior finance ministry \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  official, said in a parliamentary session. "If this market exerts considerable effects on our price stability target of 2%, and if we judge action is needed, certainly we are going to undertake additional easing measures just as we will in response to other factors."\par \par \uc2 Rises in the yen sap inflationary pressure by pushing down the prices of imported products and hurting the profitability and competitiveness of exporters.\par \par \uc2 Speculation has been mounting that should the yen resume a rise, the onus to stop it will likely fall on Mr. Kuroda as Tokyo finds other countermeasures--including direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market--hard to take because of international tensions over \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies.\par \par \uc2 U.S. and European officials have warned \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  against \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying it would spark a potentially devastating global race to devalue \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Write to Takashi Nakamichi at takashi.nakamichi@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 (MORE TO FOLLOW) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 25, 2016 00:43 ET (04:43 GMT)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 25-05-16 0518GMT\par \par \uc2 Dokument RTNW000020160525ec5p0005u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
