\par\par \b \uc2 RPT-Behind  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  threats, a calmer view of the yen\b0\par\par\uc2 777 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Mai 2016\par 01:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2016 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Repeats article first published late on Thursday. No changes to text.)\par \par \par \par \uc2 * Officials don't see serious harm from current yen levels\par \par \par \par \uc2 * Aso more worried about volatility than exchange rate\par \par \par \par \uc2 * Markets sensitive to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  threats\par \par \par \par \uc2 By Izumi Nakagawa\par \par \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, May 19 (Reuters) - Publicly, Japanese policymakers have railed against the yen's rapid appreciation to 18-month highs, putting investors on high alert against possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets.\par \par \par \par \uc2 Behind the scenes, though, those running economic policy have told Reuters they're not so worried that the yen will derail efforts to revive exports and the economy.\par \par \par \par \uc2 Those more sanguine views suggest markets might be overestimating the likelihood of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \par \par \uc2 "I don't think you can simply say the yen's rise is a bad thing," one government official told Reuters, declining to be named due to the sensitivity of the matter.\par \par \par \par \uc2 International differences over \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  could be a focus at a meeting of \uc2 Group of Seven\uc2  finance leaders in Japan this weekend.\par \par \par \par \uc2 And to be sure, concerns about the strong yen are real. The safe-haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallies during periods of market anxiety and uncertainty, having done so even after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's unexpected shift to negative interest rates this year.\par \par \par \par \uc2 Toyota Motor President and CEO \uc2 Akio Toyoda\uc2  has warned \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  losses could wipe as much as 935 billion yen ($8.5 billion) from the automaker's operating profit this year, noting that each 1 yen move against the dollar affects its operating profit by 40 billion yen.\par \par \par \par \uc2 When an economic heavyweight like Toyota reports such severe \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  effects, the government must be seen to act.\par \par \par \par \uc2 So far, Finance Minister \uc2 Taro Aso\uc2 's response has been to condemn rapid rises in the yen and threaten to step into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market - despite international objections to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \par \par \uc2 However, the view is spreading among economic officials close to the Prime Minister's Office that the yen in its recent range of 105-109 to the dollar would not upset economic recovery.\par \par \par \par \uc2 At 110 to the dollar on Thursday, the yen is trading considerably weaker than its comparative purchasing power of 103, according to valuations that look at consumer price ratios between countries.\par \par \par \par \uc2 Even in the Finance Ministry, which runs Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy, few officials express concern that the yen's strength will stifle growth.\par \par \par \par \uc2 Rather, Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  mandarins fret more over the speed of exchange rate moves than the actual level. A Finance Ministry official told Reuters that Aso, while warning against volatility, has not commented on the exchange rate, which Aso says is set by the market.\par \par \par \par \uc2 A POINT OF CONTENTION\par \par \par \par \uc2 At a meeting of the \uc2 Group of 20\uc2  big economies last month, Aso told U.S. Treasury Secretary Jack Lew of Tokyo's "strong concern" over "one-sided" yen rises. Lew fired back that he saw no "disorderly" moves in the market that might justify \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and said it was vital to avoid "beggar-thy-neighbour exchange rate policies".\par \par \par \par \uc2 While a Lew-Aso divide may attract headlines from this weekend's meeting of G7 finance ministers and central bankers in Sendai, northern Japan, officials expect the group to paper over differences by repeating general calls for exchange rate stability.\par \par \par \par \uc2 The yen has swung wildly since late 2012, when Prime Minister \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2  came to power promoting easy-money "Abenomics" policies to boost Japan from two decades of deflation and fitful growth. The yen sank 37 percent to 13-year lows on massive \uc2 Bank of Japan\uc2  (BOJ) yen-printing by June 2015.\par \par \par \par \uc2 This month, it rebounded 19 percent to 105.55, its strongest since October 2014, spurred by the BOJ's surprise decision not to ease policy further.\par \par \par \par \uc2 Some market participants worry about a knock-on effect of a higher yen hitting profits, battering stock prices further, and undoing more of the gains of "Abenomics".\par \par \par \par \uc2 "There is growing unease about the outlook for the Japanese economy, which has been supported by the weak yen," said Shingo Ide, chief equity strategist at NLI Research Institute.\par \par \par \par \uc2 Market participants think 100 yen to the dollar is the 'red line' for Japan's policymakers, a Reuters survey of some 70 \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategists found this month.\par \par \par \par \uc2 An Abe adviser, Yale University professor emeritus Koichi Hamada, told Reuters last week that if the yen strengthened to 90-95 to the dollar, "\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , even if it angers the United States."  ($1 = 109.99 yen)\par \par \par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Izumi Nakagawa; Additional reporting by Daiki Iga; Writing by Kaori Kaneko; Editing by William Mallard, Eric Meijer and Ian Geoghegan)\par \par \uc2 Released: 2016-5-22T23:00:01.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020160519ec5j02aep\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
