\par\par \b \uc2 Nikkei May Be Supported by a Recovery in Oil Prices -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,579 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Mai 2016\par 01:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2016, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 19:27 EDT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] Japanese stocks may be supported by a continuing recovery in crude oil prices. Oil prices rose to new 2016 highs Monday as production outages persisted. Sharp falls in commodity prices rocked the markets globally over the past few months. Gains in crude are particularly positive for oil producers and the banks that lend to the energy businesses. Nikkei 225 June futures ended Chicago trading at 16610 on Monday, compared to an earlier close in Osaka at 16520. Nikkei ended up 0.3% at 16466.40.(kosaku.narioka@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 2308 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ]--\b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders will browse the summary of the Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's most recent policy-board meeting, due at 0130GMT, for any hints that more interest-rate cuts may be in stall. The Australian dollar might weaken in response, even if signals for further cuts may be very subtle, says BK Asset Management in New York. "AUD shrugged off this weekend's softer industrial production and retail sales reports but it may not be able to ignore dovish RBA minutes," says BK. AUD/USD was last trading at US$0.7289 early Tuesday in Asia. (vera.sprothen@wsj.com; @verasydney)\par \par \uc2 2307 GMT -- The Australian dollar remained firm overnight, rising above its 200-day moving average, says Elias Haddad, strategist at CBA. Supporting the Australian dollar was a lift in most major global equity markets and commodity prices. At 0130 GMT, minutes of the RBA's May 3 policy meeting are due out. Haddad says that given the detail in the RBA's Statement on Monetary Policy, published just days after the policy meeting, the minutes won't provide much additional information. CBA expects a further 50 basis points of rate cuts by the RBA in 2016, which will continue to weigh on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . (james.glynn@wsj.com; Twitter @JamesGlynnWSJ)\par \par \uc2 23:05 GMT [\uc2 Dow Jones\uc2 ] The USD/JPY (now at 109.10) will likely remain directionless in a 108.70-109.20 range during Asia trade, given a lack of fresh trading cues, says Kosuke Hanao, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  at \uc2 HSBC\uc2  in Tokyo. "Investors are waiting for fresh incentives," says Mr. Hanao. Japan's January-March GDP data, due out Wednesday, may not provide a catalyst to move the USD/JPY, as fiscal, monetary stimulus and sales tax postponement by the Japanese government coming after the \uc2 G-7\uc2  summit (May 26-27) are largely factored in among many investors. But surprisingly downbeat GDP data may prompt selling of Tokyo stocks to cause a risk-off mood, he says. Mr. Hanao also tips the EUR/USD (now at 1.1317) to move in a tight 1.1300-1.1340 range. (hiroyuki.kachi@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 15:52 ET - US is pushing China to wind down its excess manufacturing capacity, particularly in the metals sector where too much production continues to keep global prices weak and undermine American sales. \uc2 US Treasury\uc2  Secretary \uc2 Jacob Lew\uc2  told Chinese Vice Premier Wang Yang that Beijing needs to "reduce excess industrial capacity in China's key base metals sectors, and establish a new set of official export credit disciplines to create a level playing field for US exporters," \uc2 Treasury\uc2  said in a readout of a call between the two officials. Economists warn that China's still keeping unproductive firms online as part of its strategy to keep the economy from cooling too fast. Not only does that create new risks for the world's second largest economy, it harms US industry. The issue will be a top focus when officials from the two countries meet for the regular US-China Strategic & Economic Dialogue next month in Beijing. (ian.talley@wsj.com; @iantalley)\par \par \uc2 15:43 ET - The auction for \uc2 Sports Authority\uc2 's inventory kicked off on Monday, with two groups of liquidators battling it out, people familiar with the matter said. A consortium of Hilco Global, \uc2 Tiger Capital Group\uc2  and \uc2 Gordon Brothers Group\uc2  is bidding against a rival group that includes SB Capital Group, Yellen Partners, \uc2 Great American Group\uc2  and 360 Merchant Solutions will battle it out through Monday, and Tuesday if needed, the people added. Following the sale of inventory, an auction for \uc2 Sports Authority\uc2 's store leases will take place. \uc2 Sports Authority\uc2  already won court approval to liquidate 140 of its 450 stores. Those closing sales were conducted Tiger Capital and \uc2 Gordon Brothers\uc2 . (lillian.rizzo@wsj.com; @lilliannnn)\par \par \uc2 14:51 ET - University of Chicago finance professor Luigi Zingales says at a \uc2 Minneapolis Fed\uc2  symposium that a simple approach which separates retail and investment banking, akin to Glass-Steagall (repealed in 1999), would help create a safer banking system. He argued that splitting up banking interests would force financial institutions to lobby more competitively in DC, making firms less powerful. "Concentrated interests have more power than diffuse interests," he told an audience which included Bernanke and St. Louis Fed chief Bullard, in addition to host Kashkari. "By fragmenting the banking industry, it will create more competition in Washington, and that will create better regulation." (shayndi.raice@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 13:59 ET - \uc2 TerraForm Global\uc2  (GLBL) says bondholders moved too soon to warn of a possible default stemming from delayed financial reports. An offshoot of troubled solar-power developer \uc2 SunEdison\uc2 , GLBL contends a bondholder notice was ineffective to start a countdown toward debt default. GLBL and another former \uc2 SunEdison\uc2  subsidiary, \uc2 TerraForm Power\uc2  (TERP) were spun out to operate completed alternative-power projects. Unlike \uc2 SunEdison\uc2 , which is mired in debt, the spinoffs are solvent. But like \uc2 SunEdison\uc2 , however, they have delayed filing audited 2015 financial reports and investors are getting impatient. GLBL is down 52% this year while TERP has fallen 28%. (peg.brickley@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 13:43 ET - Bernanke once said of \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bond buying that "the problem with QE is that it works in practice but it doesn't work in theory." Central bankers generally agree that Fed QE did work even if the exact amount of economic benefit has proved very hard to measure. A new paper today from the National Bureau for Economic Research agrees with Fed officials, saying bond buying can indeed boost inflation expectations. That said, the paper finds some challenges. "The needed \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is incredibly high, creating a serious limitation of this solution to the liquidity trap. Our experiments suggest that while asset purchases can be a helpful commitment device in theory, they may need to be combined in practice with fiscal policy coordination to achieve the desired outcome." (michael.derby@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 13:03 ET - US is still trying to broker Greek bailout deal that includes debt relief despite growing signs Europe will have to move ahead without a restructuring and the \uc2 IMF\uc2 . "All of the parties should come together and find a way forward that results in Greece receiving the financial support and debt relief it needs to make its reform program a successful one," a senior \uc2 US Treasury\uc2  official says. Secretary \uc2 Jacob Lew\uc2  will press German Finance Minister \uc2 Wolfgang Schauble\uc2  at the upcoming \uc2 G-7\uc2  meeting this week to relent and give Greece debt relief. But given the \uc2 IMF\uc2  doesn't appear ready to make 1+1=3 for a bailout program that doesn't add up without debt relief, some analysts see the \uc2 IMF\uc2  may be out of a deal, and along with it, any chance of restructuring. "The 24 May Eurogroup will conclude Greece's first review and disburse funds; It's becoming more likely this will happen without the \uc2 IMF\uc2 , delaying if not killing debt relief for Greece," says Mujtaba Rahman, head of \uc2 Eurasia Group\uc2 's Europe department. (ian.talley@wsj.com; @iantalley)\par \par \uc2 13:00 ET - Although US officials won't say it outright in public, Washington is clearly signaling to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  any yen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  right now would violate the Tokyo's exchange rate commitments to the \uc2 G-7\uc2 . "It's notable that exchange markets in recent months have been orderly," a senior \uc2 US Treasury\uc2  official says ahead of the \uc2 G-7\uc2  meeting later this week. That's a technical reference to \uc2 G-7\uc2  and G-20 statements that give countries room to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the event of "disorderly" exchange rate movements. Since the US sees the yen's appreciation as "orderly," it's telling Tokyo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would contravene their commitment and could spark a global \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  war, including a depreciation by China. "Those are very important commitments for all members of the G-20 to continue to adhere to, and it's particularly important countries in the \uc2 G-7\uc2  as leaders of the global economy," the US official says. (ian.talley@wsj.com; @iantalley)\par \par \uc2 12:49 ET - The bankruptcy of Hillview, Ky.--the first city to file for Chapter 9 protection after Detroit's historic case--has ended with a judge granting the town's request to drop the case after city leaders reached a repayment deal on its largest debt. The Louisville suburb plans to raise taxes and borrow $5M to pay off a decade-old property dispute with a truck-driver training school. The legal award won by the school, which grew by $3,759.54/day in interest, prompted Hillview leaders to put the 9K-resident municipality into bankruptcy proceedings in August. (katy.stech@wsj.com; @katystech)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 May 16, 2016 19:27 ET (23:27 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020160516ec5g004bz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
